hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3601","357 - Humayd ibn Thawr al-Hilali. 3602 - Narrated Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani from Hashim ibn al-Qasim al-Harrani: Yala ibn al-Ashdaq ibn Jarad narrated: Humayd ibn Thawr al-Hilali narrated to me that when he accepted Islam he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and recited to him: Khidabb."
"3602","3602 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated from Sufyan from Ata ibn al-Saib from Malik ibn al-Harith from a man - al-Hadrami said: in the book of Abu Kurayb, from Humayd, who said: from a man - who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed a man over a detachment; when he went and returned to him he said to him: How did you find command? He said: I was as one of the folk - when I mounted they mounted, when I dismounted they dismounted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The holder of authority is at the gate of distress except whom Allah, mighty and majestic, protects. The man said: By Allah, I will never work for you nor for any other. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed till his molars appeared."
"3603","3603 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Minjab ibn al-Harith: Sharik narrated from Ata ibn al-Saib from Khaythamah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man over a detachment; then he mentioned the like of it."
"3604","358 - Hubaysh ibn Khalid al-Khuzai. 3605 - Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, and narrated Musa ibn Harun al-Hammal, Ali ibn Saeed al-Razi and Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji, all saying: Mukram ibn Muhriz ibn Mahdi ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Khuwaylid ibn Halif ibn Munqidh ibn Rabiah ibn Manbash ibn Haram ibn Hubshiyyah ibn Kab ibn Amr ibn Harithah ibn Thalabah ibn al-Azd Abu al-Qasim al-Khuzai, then al-Rabi, narrated: my father Muhriz ibn Mahdi narrated to me from Hizam ibn Hisham ibn Khalid from his father Hisham ibn Hubaysh from his father Hubaysh ibn Khalid, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Makkah emigrating to Madinah - he, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Abu Bakr's freedman Amir ibn Fuhayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), and their guide al-Laythi Abd Allah ibn al-Urayqit - they passed the two tents of Umm Mabad al-Khuzaiyyah. She was a mature, sturdy woman sitting at the tent-yard, giving drink and food. They asked her for meat and dates to buy, but found nothing of that with her; the folk were without provisions, in drought. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a ewe in the tent's corner and said: What is this ewe, O Umm Mabad? She said: Weakness kept it from the flock. He said: Is there milk in it? She said: It is too exhausted for that. He said: Do you permit me to milk it? She said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you; if you see milk in it, milk it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for it, wiped its udder with his hand, named Allah, mighty and majestic, and supplicated for it concerning her ewe. It spread its legs for him, yielded milk and flowed... [long Umm Mabad hadith; remainder truncated in source extract]."
"3605","358 - Hubaysh ibn Khalid al-Khuzai. Hubaysh ibn Khalid, Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), reported: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Makkah emigrating to Madinah - he, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), Abu Bakr's freedman Amir ibn Fuhayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), and their guide al-Laythi Abd Allah ibn al-Urayqit - they passed the two tents of Umm Mabad al-Khuzaiyyah. She was a mature, sturdy woman sitting at the tent-yard, giving drink and food. They asked her for meat and dates to buy, but found nothing of that with her; the folk were without provisions, in drought. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a ewe in the tent's corner and said: What is this ewe, O Umm Mabad? She said: Weakness kept it from the flock. He said: Is there milk in it? She said: It is too exhausted for that. He said: Do you permit me to milk it? She said: Yes, may my father and mother be ransom for you; if you see milk in it, milk it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for it, wiped its udder with his hand, named Allah, mighty and majestic, and supplicated for it concerning her ewe. It spread its legs for him, yielded milk and flowed. He called for a vessel that would satisfy a group, and milked into it copiously till foam rose. Then he gave her to drink till she was quenched, gave his companions till they were quenched, and drank last of them (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then they rested, then he milked into it a second time after the first till he filled the vessel, left it with her, pledged her and departed. Soon after, her husband Abu Mabad came driving lean goats, staggering from thinness in the forenoon, their marrow scant. When Abu Mabad saw the milk he marveled and said: Whence is this milk for you, O Umm Mabad, when the ewe is away grazing and barren, and there is no milch beast in the house? She said: No, by Allah, except that a blessed man passed us, of such and such state. He said: Describe him to me, O Umm Mabad. She said: I saw a man of manifest radiance, bright-faced, fair in form; no belly faulted him nor small head belittled him; comely, in his eyes intense black-and-white, in his lashes length, in his voice huskiness, in his neck loftiness, in his beard fullness; arched-browed, joined; if silent, dignity upon him, if speaking, splendor raised him; most beautiful and radiant of men from afar, sweetest and finest near; sweet of speech, decisive, neither babbling nor meager, as if his words beads of a necklace cascading; middle-statured, neither despaired of for tallness nor scorned by the eye for shortness; a branch between two branches, the freshest of the three in look and finest in rank; companions surround him - if he speaks they listen to his word, if he commands they race to his command; served, gathered-about, neither frowning nor discredited. Abu Mabad said: By Allah, he is the companion of Quraysh whose affair was told us at Makkah; I had resolved to accompany him and shall if I find a way. A voice rose at Makkah, high, while they heard the voice knowing not its owner, saying [verses omitted in source extract]. When Hassan ibn Thabit heard that, he answered the caller with verse [fragment preserved in source]. Musa ibn Harun added in his hadith: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us from Mukram, who told us variant wordings of the description (thujlah/saqla vs thuhlah/sala): the correct is thujlah (bigness of belly) and sala (smallness of head) - meaning he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither big-bellied nor small-headed; and variants wataf (length of lashes) and sahal (hoarseness); and la yabasa min tul (corrected: not over-tall); and la abis wa la mufannad, meaning neither frowning nor belied. [isnad, via key 3605: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz; Musa ibn Harun al-Hammal, Ali ibn Saeed al-Razi, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji - all from Mukram ibn Muhriz ibn Mahdi al-Khuzai, from his father Muhriz ibn Mahdi, from Hizam ibn Hisham ibn Khalid, from his father Hisham ibn Hubaysh, from his father Hubaysh ibn Khalid]."
"3606","3606 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Marzuq: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated: my father narrated to me from Thumamah ibn Abd Allah ibn Anas from Anas: people of Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him to send with them men to teach them the Quran. He sent with them seventy men of the Ansar, among them Haram ibn Milhan, uncle of Anas. They betrayed them and killed them. Haram was the first stabbed with a short spear; blood flowed from him, and he caught it, raised it to heaven and said: I have won, by the Lord of the Kabah. Concerning them Quran came down: Convey from us that we met our Lord and He was pleased with us and pleased us."
"3607","3607 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman: Ishaq Abu al-Harith narrated, saying: I saw Hashraj, a man the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took, placed in his lap, wiped his head and supplicated for him."
"3608","Hanifah al-Raqashi, uncle of Abu Hurrah. 3609 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan from Abu Hurrah al-Raqashi from his uncle, who said: I held the halter of the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the middle days of al-Tashriq in the Farewell Hajj, and he mentioned the hadith."
"3609","3609 - Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna from Musaddad: Abu Awanah narrated from Dawud ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari: a man called Humamah, of the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), went campaigning to Isbahan in the caliphate of Umar (may Allah be pleased with him); Isbahan was conquered, and Humamah said: O Allah, Humamah claims he loves meeting You; if he is truthful, decree it upon him for his truthfulness, and if lying, decree it upon him though he dislike it. Dysentery seized him and he died at Isbahan. Abu Musa said: O people, by Allah, of what we heard from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and what reached our knowledge, Humamah is but a martyr."
"3610","Chapter of Kha. 364 - Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, a Badri, kunyah Abu Abd Allah, ally of Banu Zuhrah ibn Kilab ibn Murrah ibn Kab ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr; and it is said: freedman of Banu Zuhrah. His lineage is disputed; whoever ascribes him to the Arabs claims he is of Tamim ibn Murr ibn Talhah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar. 3611 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani: my father narrated to me: Ibn Lahiah narrated from Abu al-Aswad from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr: among those who witnessed Badr: Khabbab ibn al-Aratt ibn Khuwaylid ibn Sad ibn Jadhimah ibn Kab ibn Sad."
"3611","3611 - Narrated Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated from al-Zubaydi from al-Zuhri, who said: Khabbab ibn al-Aratt was a freedman of Banu Zuhrah, witnessed Badr, kunyah Abu Abd Allah; he died in the year thirty-seven upon Ali's (may Allah be pleased with him) return from Siffin to Kufah. He was the first buried at Kufah of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Khabbab's Islam was at Makkah."
"3612","3612 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated from his father, saying: I heard Kurdus say: Khabbab accepted Islam as the sixth of six; he was a sixth of Islam."
"3613","3613 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Hulwani: Yahya ibn Adam narrated: Waki narrated from his father from Abu Ishaq from Madi Karib, who said: We came to Abd Allah ibn Masud asking him about Ta-Sin-Mim, the Poets. He said: It is not with me; but upon you is one who took it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): upon you is Abu Abd Allah Khabbab ibn al-Aratt."
"3614","3614 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban: Abu Usamah narrated from Idris al-Awdi from al-Minhal ibn Amr from Abu Wail, who said: I entered upon Khabbab, and he said: In this chest are eighty thousand, no cord tied for them nor withheld from a beggar; I wish they were so-and-so - either he said dung or otherwise."
"3615","3615 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Abu Kurayb: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated: Misar narrated from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: Remnants of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Khabbab and said: Glad tidings, O Abu Abd Allah; your brothers - you come upon them tomorrow. He wept then said: Those passed with their rewards, and I fear my reward for those deeds is what we were given after them."
"3616","3616 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr: Talq ibn Ghannam narrated from Yunus ibn Ikrimah: Khabbab bequeathed to be buried in the outskirts of the folk of Kufah."
"3617","3617 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti: Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated from al-Amash from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: We marched with him, meaning Ali, when he returned from Siffin until at the gate of Kufah we saw seven graves to our right. Ali said: What are these graves? They said: O Commander of the Believers, Khabbab ibn al-Aratt died after your departure to Siffin and bequeathed to be buried in the outskirts of Kufah; people used to bury their dead in their courtyards and at their doors, but when they saw Khabbab bequeath burial in the outskirts, people buried there. Ali said: May Allah have mercy on Khabbab; he accepted Islam willingly, emigrated obediently, lived striving, and was tried in his body with trials; Allah never wastes the reward of the doers of good. Then he drew near the graves and said: Peace upon you, O folk of the abodes, of believers and Muslims; you are our predecessors gone before, and we, your followers, shall soon join you. O Allah, forgive us and them, and pardon us and them by Your pardon. Blessed is whoever remembered the Return, worked for the Reckoning, sufficed with little, and was pleased with Allah, mighty and majestic."
"3618","What Khabbab ibn al-Aratt transmitted; Abu Umamah al-Bahili from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt. 3619 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, who said: I and a group with me entered upon Khabbab ibn al-Aratt (may Allah have mercy on him) while he had cauterized his side. We said: You cauterized? He said: Yes; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Seventy thousand of my ummah enter Paradise without reckoning: they do not charm, nor seek charms, nor cauterize, and upon their Lord they rely."
"3619","3619 - Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih from Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us from Ubayd Allah ibn Zahr from Ali ibn Yazid from al-Qasim from Abu Umamah from Khabbab, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No spending a believer spends but is rewarded in it, except spending in this dust."
"3620","Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from his father. 3621 - Narrated Abu Zuraah and Musa ibn Isa, both saying: Abu al-Yaman narrated: Shuayb narrated, and narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi from Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi: Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated from al-Zuhri from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from his father Khabbab: he watched the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night; he prayed till near dawn and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you tonight pray a prayer I never saw you pray the like of? He said: Yes; it is a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, three traits: He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy us as He destroyed the nations, and He gave me that. I asked Him not to set an enemy over us to destroy us, and He gave me that. I asked Him not to clothe my ummah in factions, and He withheld it."
"3621","3621 - Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal: my father narrated to me: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated: my father narrated to me from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ibn Shihab: Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal informed me from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab ibn al-Aratt: Khabbab said: I observed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a prayer he prayed till near dawn; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saluted from his prayer, Khabbab stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you, you prayed tonight a prayer I never saw you pray the like of? He said: Yes; it is a prayer of hope and fear. I asked in it my Lord, mighty and majestic, three traits: He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy us as He destroyed the nations before us, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to raise over us an enemy other than us, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to clothe us in factions, and He withheld it from me."
"3622","3622 - Narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated: my father narrated to me, saying: I heard al-Numan ibn Rashid narrate from al-Zuhri from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab ibn al-Aratt from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer and lengthened it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed a prayer you never used to pray? He said: Yes; it is a prayer of hope and fear. I asked my Lord in it three things: He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy my ummah by drought, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to set over them an enemy other than them, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to make them taste one another's might, and He withheld it from me."
"3623","3623 - Narrated Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Mustamli from Ali ibn al-Madini: Abd al-Razzaq narrated: Mamar informed us from al-Zuhri from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from his father, saying: I observed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I will see how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prays. He prayed; when he finished I came from before him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you prayed tonight a prayer I never saw you pray the like of. He said: It is a prayer of awe and hope. I asked my Lord in it three things: He gave me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy us as He destroyed the nations before us, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to set an enemy over us, and He gave it to me. I asked Him not to clothe us in factions, and He withheld it from me."
"3624","3624 - Narrated Amr ibn Ishaq ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi from his father: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated: Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated from al-Zubaydi from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3625","Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it - it is a prayer of hope and fear; I asked my Lord in it three things: He gave me two and withheld one. [isnad, via key 3625: Amr ibn Ishaq ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi from his father: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated; Abd Allah ibn Salim narrated from al-Zubaydi from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from his father]."
"3626","3626 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"3627","3627 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Muadh narrated to us, (Ha), and Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ubaydullah al-Ghudani narrated to us, they both said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abu Yunus al-Qushayri, Hatim ibn Abi Saghirrah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from his father, he said: We were sitting at the door of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he came out to us and said: Do you hear? We said: We have heard, twice or thrice. Then he said: There will be rulers over you, so do not affirm them in their lies, and do not help them in their wrongdoing; for whoever affirms them in their lies against their wrongdoing will not come to me at the Hawd."
"3628","3628 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Imran ibn Bakkar al-Barrad al-Himsi narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Rawh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from Adi ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tai, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Harb, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Hatim ibn Abi Saghirrah."
"3629","3629 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (Ha), and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, they both said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, a man from Abd al-Qays who used to sit with us in the congregational mosque narrated to us, he said: I accompanied the people of al-Nahr, and I was among them, then I disliked their affair; I feared they would kill me. While I was with a group of them, we came upon a village, and between us and the village was a river, when a man came out of the village frightened. They said to him: It is as if we frightened you? He said: Yes. They said: No fright upon you. I said: By Allah, they knew him, but I did not know him. They said: Are you Ibn Khabbab, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. They said: Did you hear from your father a hadith you can narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I heard my father narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he mentioned a tribulation and said: The one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing in it is better than the one walking, and the one walking in it is better than the one striving. If it reaches you, then be the slain servant of Allah. He said: So they brought him near to the bank of the river and slaughtered him; I saw his blood flowing in the water like a sandal strap, without clotting. He said: Then they took his umm walad and killed her, and she was pregnant, and they ripped open her belly. I never accompanied people whose companionship was more hateful to me than theirs, until I found a moment alone and escaped."
"3630","3630 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Ismail ibn Maslamah ibn Qanab narrated to us, my father Maslamah narrated to me, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from a man from Abd al-Qays, he said: I was with the Khawarij, and we came upon a man. They said: Are you Abdullah ibn Khabbab, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. They said: Will you narrate to us from your father from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I heard my father narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will be a tribulation; the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing in it is better than the one walking, and the one walking in it is better than the one striving. When that happens, then be the slain servant of Allah. They said to him: Then you be the slain servant of Allah. He said: So they brought him forward to the edge of the river and struck his neck; his blood flowed as if it were a sandal strap, without clotting. Then they brought his umm walad near and ripped open what was in her belly. When I saw that, I left them."
"3631","3631 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Said ibn Amir narrated to us, from Salih ibn Rustum, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from a man from Abd al-Qays, he said: When the people split, I accompanied a people whose companionship was never more beloved to me; we traveled along the bank of a river, and a mosque was raised before us, and in it was a man. When he saw the forelocks of the horses, he came out frightened, dragging his garment. Our leader said to him: You were not frightened. He said: You have frightened me. He said: And he was Abdullah ibn Khabbab. Our leader said to him: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from your father, he narrates it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a tribulation: the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, and the one standing in it is better than the one walking, and the one walking in it is better than the one striving. If it reaches you, then be the slain servant of Allah. He said: So they brought him near to the bank of the river and slaughtered him; I saw his blood flowing in the water like a sandal strap, without clotting. He said: Then they took his umm walad and killed her, and she was pregnant, and they ripped open her belly. I never accompanied a people more hateful to me than them, until I found a moment alone and escaped."
"3632","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Khabbab; Ismail ibn Abi Khalid from Qays. 3632 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ali ibn Mabad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I visited Khabbab to see him while ill, and he had been cauterized seven times on his belly. Khabbab said: Were it not that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to supplicate for death, I would have supplicated for it. Indeed our companions passed on and did not attain anything of this world; we have attained after them until we find no place for it except in the dust. A man is rewarded for all his spending except for something he puts into this dust. He said: And on that day he was building a wall of his."
"3633","3633 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: We came to Khabbab to visit him while ill, and he had been cauterized seven times on his belly. He said: Were it not that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade supplicating for death, I would have supplicated for it. Then he mentioned those of his companions who passed: they passed and did not consume anything of their rewards, while we remained after them until we attained of this world what none of us knows what to do with except to spend it in the dust. A Muslim is rewarded for everything he spends except what he spends in the dust."
"3634","3634 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, he said: I came to Khabbab, and he had been cauterized seven times on his belly. He said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to supplicate for death, I would have supplicated for it."
"3635","3635 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Ismail, from Qays, he said: We visited Khabbab to see him while ill, and he had been cauterized with seven cauterizations. He said: Our companions who preceded us passed on and left; the world did not diminish them in anything, while we attained after them what we find no place for except the dust. He said: Then we came after that to visit him while he was building a wall of his. He said: A Muslim is rewarded for everything he spends except something he puts into the dust; were it not that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, or forbade us, to supplicate for death, I would have supplicated for it."
"3636","3636 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they both said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: We visited Khabbab, and he had been cauterized seven times on his belly. He said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to supplicate for death, I would have supplicated for it."
"3637","3637 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak and Waki narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"3638","3638 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ismail, Qays narrated to us, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, he said: We complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Kabah. We said: Will you not seek victory for us, will you not supplicate for us? He said: Among those before you, a man would be taken and combed with combs of iron, beyond his flesh and bone, yet that would not turn him away from his religion. By Allah, this affair will surely be completed until a rider travels from Sanaa to Hadramawt, fearing none except Allah, or the wolf for his sheep; but you are hasty."
"3639","3639 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Khabbab, he said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on his cloak in the shade of the Kabah, and we complained to him. We said: Will you not seek victory for us, will you not supplicate to Allah for us? He said: He sat up with his color reddened, and said: Among those before you, a man would be taken and a pit dug for him in the ground, then a saw brought and placed upon his head, splitting him into two halves; it would not turn him from his religion. By Allah, Allah will surely complete this affair until a rider travels from Sanaa to Hadramawt, fearing none except Allah and the wolf for his sheep; but you are hasty."
"3640","3639 / 2 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from Khabbab, he said: We visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Kabah. We said: Will you not supplicate for us? He sat up with his face reddened, and said: Among those before you, a man would be taken and a pit dug for him in the ground, then a saw brought and placed over his head; it would not turn him from his religion. He would be combed with combs of iron, beneath his bone, of flesh and sinew, yet it would not turn him from his religion. Allah will surely complete this affair until a rider travels from Sanaa to Hadramawt, fearing none except Allah and the wolf for his sheep; but you are hasty."
"3641","3640 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from Khabbab, he said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a cloak of his in the shade of the Kabah. We said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate to Allah, will you not seek victory? He sat up with his face reddened in anger, then said: Among those before you, one of them would have a pit dug for him, then placed in it, then a saw placed upon his head, then combed with combs of iron beneath his bone; that would not turn him from his religion. But you are hasty. By Allah, this affair will surely be completed until a rider travels from Sanaa to Hadramawt, fearing none except Allah and the wolf for his sheep."
"3642","3641 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Mahri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash informed me, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every spending a servant spends is rewarded therein except building."
"3643","3642 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, they both said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, he said: Khabbab used to place the short spear for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3644","3643 - Al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani and Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, they both said: al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Khabbab, he said: I used to place the short spear for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3645","Isa ibn al-Musayyab from Qays. 3644 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: We visited Khabbab while he had been cauterized. He said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3646","3644 / 2 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isa ibn al-Musayyab, from Qays, he said: We visited Khabbab while he had been cauterized seven times. He said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3647","Bayan ibn Bishr from Qays ibn Abi Hazim. 3645 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Umar ibn Ismail ibn Mujalid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Bayan ibn Bishr and Ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, he said: We visited Khabbab to see him while ill, and he had been cauterized. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to supplicate for death; were it not for that, I would have supplicated. While he was repairing a wall of his, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Muslim is rewarded for all his spending except what he puts into the dust."
"3648","3646 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid and Bayan ibn Bishr, from Qays, from Khabbab, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a cloak in the shade of the Kabah, and we had met severe hardship from the polytheists. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate to Allah for us? He sat up angered, his face reddened, and said: Among those before you, one would be asked for the word and not grant it, then a saw placed upon him, splitting him in two; that would not turn him from his religion. One of them would be combed beneath his bones, of flesh or sinew, with combs of iron; that would not turn him from his religion. But you are hasty. Allah will surely complete this affair until a rider travels from Sanaa to Hadramawt, fearing none except Allah; Bayan added therein: or the wolf for his sheep."
"3649","3647 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ismail and Bayan, from Qays, he said: I heard Khabbab ibn al-Aratt saying: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was reclining on a cloak in the shade of the Kabah, and we had met severe hardship from the polytheists, and they had brought us to exhaustion. I said: Will you not supplicate for us? He said: Among those before you, a man would be taken and combed with iron beneath his flesh and bone; that would not turn him from his religion."
"3650","Al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri from Qays ibn Abi Hazim. 3648 - Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Wakii narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mughirah, from Qays, from Khabbab, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was lying under a tree, placing his hand under his head. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate to Allah against these people, whom we fear will turn us back from our religion? He said: He turned his face away from me; I moved toward him, and he turned his face away from me, three times; each time I said it to him and he turned his face away from me. He sat up on the third time, then said: O people, fear Allah; by Allah, a believing man before you would have a saw placed upon his head, splitting him in two, yet he would not turn back from his religion. Fear Allah, for Allah Almighty will surely grant you victory and will act."
"3651","3649 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"3652","Masruq ibn al-Ajda from Khabbab. 3650 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, they both said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Khabbab, he said: I was a blacksmith in the pre-Islamic period, and I made a sword for al-As ibn Wail. I came to demand payment from him, and he said: I will not give you until you disbelieve in Muhammad. I said: I will not disbelieve in Muhammad until Allah causes you to die. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah Almighty revealed: Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses and said: I shall surely be given wealth and children. Did he look into the unseen, or take a covenant with the Most Merciful. He said: as a documented covenant."
"3653","3651 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Sulayman al-Amash, he said: I heard Abu al-Duha narrating from Masruq, from Khabbab, he said: I was a blacksmith in the pre-Islamic period, and I had dirhams due from al-As ibn Wail. I came to demand them from him: I will not pay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad. I said: I will not disbelieve in Muhammad until Allah causes you to die, then resurrects you. He said: Leave me until I die, then am resurrected, and I come to have wealth and children, then I will pay you. He said: Then this verse was revealed: Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses and said: I shall surely be given wealth and children, to the end of the verse."
"3654","3652 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Khabbab, he said: I did work for al-As ibn Wail, then I came to demand payment from him. He said: You claim you will return to wealth and children, and I shall return to wealth and children; when you return to me there, I will give you. Then Allah Almighty revealed: Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses, the verse."
"3655","3653 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father and Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Khabbab, he said: I had a right due from al-As ibn Wail, so I came to demand it from him. He said: I will not pay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: By Allah, I will not disbelieve in him until you die and are resurrected. He said: When I am resurrected, I shall have wealth and children, then I will pay you your right. Then Allah Almighty revealed: Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses, the verse."
"3656","3654 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"3657","3655 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Muslim, from Masruq, he said: I heard Khabbab saying: I was a blacksmith, and I had something due from al-As ibn Wail, then he mentioned the hadith."
"3658","Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salamah from Masruq from Khabbab. 3656 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Ahwal narrated to us, Abu Ubaydah ibn Man al-Masudi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Masruq, he said: I heard Khabbab ibn al-Aratt saying: On the day of Uhud, Musab ibn Umayr, may Allah have mercy on him, was killed, and he left nothing except a striped cloak; when his face and head were covered with it, his feet showed, and when his feet were covered with it, his head showed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover his head with it, and place upon his feet something of idhkhir."
"3659","Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salamah from Khabbab. 3657 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab, he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking the face of Allah, so our reward became due upon Allah. Among us are those who departed without consuming any of their reward; among them was Musab ibn Umayr, killed on the day of Uhud, and he had nothing except a striped cloak; when we covered his head, his feet came out, and when we covered his feet, his head came out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cover his head with it, and place upon his feet of idhkhir. And among us are those whose fruit ripened for them, so they are gathering it."
"3660","3658 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab, he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking the face of Allah Almighty, then he mentioned similar to it."
"3661","3659 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi and Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab, he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned similar to it."
"3662","3660 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, he said: I heard Khabbab ibn al-Aratt saying: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking the face of Allah Almighty, so our reward became due upon Allah. Among us are those who passed on without consuming anything of their good deeds; among them is al-Musab ibn Umayr, killed on the day of Uhud, leaving a cloak; when we placed it upon his feet, his head showed, and when we placed it upon his head, his feet showed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that we place it upon his head, and place upon his feet something of idhkhir. And among us are those whose fruit ripened for them, so they are gathering it, meaning they eat it."
"3663","3661 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from al-Amash, he said: I heard Shaqiq ibn Salamah saying: Khabbab narrated to us, he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking the face of Allah Almighty, and our reward became due upon Allah. Among us are those who passed on without consuming anything of their reward; among them was Musab ibn Umayr, killed on the day of Uhud, and we found nothing to shroud him in except a striped cloak; when we covered his head with it, his feet came out, and when we covered his feet, his head came out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to cover his head and place idhkhir upon his feet. And among us are those whose fruit ripened for them, so they are gathering it."
"3664","3662 - Al-Hasan ibn Mansur al-Rummani al-Massisi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Muadh narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab, he said: We are a people who emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so our reward became due upon Allah. Among us are those who died without consuming anything of their reward; among them was Musab ibn Umayr, killed on the day of Uhud, and nothing was found for him except a striped cloak; when his head was covered with it, his feet came out, and when his feet were covered with it, his head came out. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Cover his head with it, and place idhkhir upon him. And among us are those whose fruit ripened for them, so they are gathering it."
"3665","3663 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Khabbab, he said: We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking the face of Allah, then he mentioned similar to it."
"3666","3664 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"3667","3665 - Ahmad ibn Ali al-Jarudi al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Zajjaj narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Khabbab, he said: I had a debt due from al-As ibn Wail, and I was a blacksmith. I came to demand it from him, and he said: I will not give you until you disbelieve in Muhammad. I said: I will not disbelieve in Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until you die, then are resurrected. He said: And shall I indeed be resurrected after death? He said: Yes. He said: Then I shall have wealth and children. He said: Then Allah Almighty revealed: Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our verses, to: alone. Abu al-Qasim said: Thus Hammad ibn Shuayb narrated it, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail; the people narrated it as we mentioned first, from al-Amash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Khabbab. If Hammad ibn Shuayb preserved it from al-Amash, then it is rare from the hadith of Abu Wail."
"3668","3666 - Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Akhram narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu al-Sari Sahl ibn Mahmud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from his father, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salamah, he said: We visited Khabbab ibn al-Aratt in his illness, and he said: In this chest are eighty thousand dirhams; by Allah, I never tied a thread for them, nor withheld them from a beggar. Then he wept. It was said: What makes you weep? He said: I weep that my companions passed on and the world did not diminish them in anything, while we remained after them until we find no place for it."
"3669","3667 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Idris al-Awdi, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Shaqiq, he said: We visited Khabbab to see him while ill, and he wept. He said: In this chest are seventy thousand; no string was tied for them, nor was a beggar withheld from them. I wish they were such-and-such; either he said: dung, or he said: other than it."
"3670","Harithah ibn Mudarrib from Khabbab. 3668 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Khabbab, he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3671","3669 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Khabbab, he said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3672","3670 - Al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ibn Ibnat al-Suddi narrated to us, (Ha), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, they both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, he said: We visited Khabbab to see him while ill, and he had been cauterized seven times on his belly. He said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3673","3671 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, he said: I visited Khabbab ibn al-Aratt while he had been cauterized seven times. He said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3674","3672 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Warkani narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, he said: We visited Khabbab while he had been cauterized seven times on his belly. He said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3675","3673 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Aslam al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, he said: We visited Khabbab, and he said: You have seen me with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) owning not a dirham, while these forty thousand lie placed here."
"3676","3674 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, he said: We visited Khabbab, and he said: You have seen me with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) owning not a dirham, while today in the side of my house there are forty thousand dirhams."
"3677","3675 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, (Ha), and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl narrated to us, they both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, he said: We visited Khabbab while in his house a wall was being built. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A believer is rewarded for his spending except for something he puts into the dust."
"3678","3676 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they both said: Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3679","3677 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (Ha), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said: Yahya ibn Isa narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of prayer in the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3680","3678 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of prayer in the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3681","3679 - Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, from Khabbab, he said: We feared that what we attained of this world after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take away our rewards."
"3682","3680 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Harithah, from Khabbab, he said: Hamzah was shrouded in a cloak; when his head was covered, his feet came out, and when his feet were covered, his head came out."
"3683","3681 - Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah, (Ha), and Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asbahani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Mudarrib, from Khabbab, he said: I saw Hamzah, and we found no garment to shroud him in other than a cloak; when we covered his feet with it, his head came out, and when we covered his head with it, his feet came out. So we covered his head and placed idhkhir upon his feet."
"3684","3682 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah, he said: We visited Khabbab, then his shroud was brought; when he saw it, he wept. Then he said: But for Hamzah, no shroud was found except a cloak; when placed upon his head, it shrank from his feet, and when placed upon his feet, it shrank from his head, until it was extended over his head and idhkhir placed upon his feet."
"3685","Abu Mamar Abdullah ibn Sakhbarah from Khabbab. 3683 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, he said: We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr? He said: Yes. We said: By what did you know? He said: By the movement of his beard."
"3686","3684 - Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, he said: We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr? He said: Yes. We said: How did you know that? He said: By the movement of his beard."
"3687","3685 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, he said: I said to Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr? He said: Yes. We said: By what did you recognize that? He said: By the movement of his beard."
"3688","3686 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3689","3687 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah and Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, he said: We said to Khabbab: By what did you recognize the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr? He said: By the movement of his beard."
"3690","3688 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah, from Abu Mamar, he said: We asked Khabbab: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite in Zuhr and Asr? He said: Yes. We said: By what did you know that? He said: By the movement of his beard."
"3691","3689 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Marwan and Abu Usamah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah ibn Umayr, from Abu Mamar, he said: We said to Khabbab: By what did you recognize the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr? He said: By the movement of his beard."
"3692","Abu Maysarah Amr ibn Shurahbil from Khabbab. 3690 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Shurahbil, he said: I visited Khabbab to see him while ill, and he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let none of you wish for death, I would have wished for it."
"3693","Hubayrah ibn Yarim from Khabbab. 3691 - Muhammad ibn Said ibn Kasa al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Khabbab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Ashura: O people, whoever among you wishes to fast this day, let him fast it; whoever has not eaten, let him complete his fast; and whoever ate, let him fast the remainder of his day."
"3694","3692 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, from Khabbab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Ashura: O people, whoever among you ate, let him not eat the remainder of his day; and whoever among you intended fasting, let him fast it."
"3695","Abu al-Kanud from Khabbab. 3693 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, they both said: Ahmad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Sad al-Azdi, from Abu al-Kanud, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, regarding His saying Almighty: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face. He said: There came, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Tamimi and Uyaynah ibn Hisn al-Fazari; they found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sitting with Bilal, Ammar ibn Yasir, Suhayb, and Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, may Allah be pleased with them, among some of the weak believers. When they saw them around him, they belittled them. They came to him and secluded him, and said: We wish you would make for us a sitting from you by which the Arabs recognize our merit; the delegations of the Arabs come to you, and we are ashamed that the Arabs see us sitting with these slaves; when we come to you, remove them from us, and when we finish, seat them if you wish. He said: Yes. They said: So write for us a document upon you. He called for the paper to write for them, and called Ali to write. When he intended that, while we were sitting aside, Jibril, peace be upon him, descended: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, the verse. Then he mentioned al-Aqra ibn Habis and his companion, He said: And thus We tried some of them with others, that they say: Are these those upon whom Allah bestowed favor from among us? Is Allah not most knowing of the grateful? Then he mentioned him and said: And when those who believe in Our verses come to you, say: Peace be upon you; your Lord has prescribed mercy upon Himself. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw away the paper, called us, and we came to him while he was saying: Peace be upon you. We drew near him until we placed our knees upon his knees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit with us; when he wished to rise, he rose and left us. Then Allah Almighty revealed: And keep yourself with those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His face, and let not your eyes pass beyond them, desiring the adornment of worldly life. That is: Do not sit with the nobles. Nor obey him whose heart We made heedless of Our remembrance, who followed his desire, and whose affair is ruin. As for the one whose heart was made heedless, it is Uyaynah and al-Aqra ibn Habis; as for ruin, it is destruction. Then he struck the example of two men and the example of worldly life. He said: After that, we would sit with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when we reached the hour in which he used to rise, we rose and left him until he rose, otherwise he waited until we rose."
"3696","Al-Shabi from Khabbab. 3694 - Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, he said: There was none except he gave what they asked on the day the polytheists tortured them, except Khabbab ibn al-Aratt; they would lay him upon the hot stones, yet they obtained nothing from him. He said: His shroud was brought, and white Egyptian cloths spread upon him, and he wept. They said: What makes you weep, O Abu Abdullah, while you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I remembered Musab ibn Umayr; he did not hasten any of his good things; he was shrouded in a cloak, and found nothing to be shrouded in; when we covered his head with it, his feet came out, and when we covered his feet, his head came out, until we placed upon him idhkhir and plants of the earth."
"3697","Yahya ibn Jadah from Khabbab. 3695 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Jadah, he said: Some companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Khabbab while ill, and said: Rejoice, O Abu Abdullah, you will come to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the Hawd. He said: How about this? And he pointed to the top of his house and to its bottom; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What suffices one of you in this world is but like the provision of a rider."
"3698","Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman from Khabbab. 3696 - Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Khalil al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Kaysan Abu Umar al-Attar narrated to us, from Yazid, meaning Ibn Bilal, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: And Kaysan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you fast, use the siwak in the morning, and do not use the siwak in the evening; for there is no fasting person whose lips dry in the evening except it shall be a light between his eyes on the Day of Resurrection. Ali did not raise it."
"3699","Mujahid from Khabbab. 3697 - Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Khabbab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in a detachment, and thirst struck us, and we had no water. A she-camel of one of us knelt, and between her legs was like a waterskin, so we drank of her milk."
"3700","Said ibn Wahb al-Hamdani from Khabbab. 3698 - Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, (Ha), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, all of them from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint; he means in the midday prayer."
"3701","3699 - Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the heat of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3702","3700 - Abu Man Thabit ibn Nuaym al-Hawji narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, (Ha), and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, they both said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3703","3701 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (Ha), and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, they both said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the severity of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint. He said: When the sun declines, then pray."
"3704","3702 - Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3705","3703 - Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Wahb, Khabbab narrated to me, he said: We complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the hot ground, but he did not relieve our complaint. He said: When the sun declines, then pray."
"3706","Sulayman ibn Abi Hind from Khabbab. 3704 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Sulayman ibn Abi Hind, from Khabbab, he said: We complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of the severity of heat upon our foreheads and palms, but he did not relieve our complaint."
"3707","Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl from Khabbab. 3705 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, they both said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Khabbab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the Children of Israil perished, they told stories."
"3708","3706 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Said Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, al-Thiqah narrated to us, from Abu Usamah, from al-Ajlah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, he said: I visited Khabbab and saw uncovered dirhams in his house. I said: What is this? He said: I sold such-and-such estate of mine, and I have spent it; I see none more deserving of it than me."
"3709","Silah ibn Zufar from Khabbab. 3707 - Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Ulayy informed me, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses are three: a horse for the Most Merciful, a horse for man, and a horse for Satan. As for the horse of the Most Merciful: what is taken in the path of Allah and His enemies fought upon it. As for the horse of man: what is kept for breeding and ridden. As for the horse of Satan: what is bet upon and gambled upon."
"3710","Abbad Abu al-Akhdar from Khabbab. 3708 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, my father and Jabir al-Jufi narrated to me, from Maqil al-Zubaydi, from Abbad Abu al-Akhdar, from Khabbab, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he never came to his bed except he recited: Say: O disbelievers, until he completed it."
"3711","Ubadah ibn Nusayy from Khabbab. 3709 - Al-Hasan ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Munir ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us that he heard Ubadah ibn Nusayy narrating from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on a mission. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you send me far, while I fear for you. He said: What is the extent of your fear for me? I said: I wake in the morning doubting you will reach evening, and I reach evening doubting you will reach morning. He said: O Khabbab, five things: if you do them, you shall see me, and if you do not do them, you shall not see me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are they? He said: Worship Allah, associating nothing with Him, even if you are cut and burned; believe in the decree. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is belief in the decree? He said: Know that what struck you was never to miss you, and what missed you was never to strike you; do not drink wine, for its sin knocks upon sins, just as its tree overtops trees; be dutiful to your parents, even if they command you to leave the world; hold fast to the rope of the community, for the hand of Allah is upon the community. O Khabbab, if you see me on the Day of Resurrection, you shall not part from me."
"3712","Khabbab Abu Ibrahim al-Khuzai. 3710 - Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from Qays, from Majzaah ibn Thawr al-Aslami, from Ibrahim ibn Khabbab al-Khuzai, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Allah, cover my nakedness, secure my fright, and settle my debt for me."
"3713","3711 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: Khuzaymah ibn Thabit fought on the day of Siffin until he was killed."
"3714","Zayd ibn Thabit from Khuzaymah. 3712 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit said: When we wrote the codices, I missed a verse I used to hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I found it with Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari: Among the believers are men who were true to what they covenanted with Allah; among them is he who fulfilled his vow, and among them is he who waits, and they did not change at all. He said: And Khuzaymah was called the one of two testimonies."
"3715","Jabir ibn Abdullah from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit. 3713 - Yaqub ibn Ghaylan al-Ammani, al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi, and al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Isa ibn al-Mukhtar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): regarding wiping for the traveler: three days, and for the resident: a day and a night."
"3716","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit. 3714 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Sadan ibn Yazid narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Ansari, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Muzdalifah with a single iqamah."
"3717","3715 - Musa ibn Sahl al-Jawni and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, they both said: Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mansur narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Abu Layla, from Jabir ibn Yazid, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Muzdalifah three and two. Abu al-Qasim said: Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, Shubah, Zuhayr, and others narrated this hadith, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Ghaylan and Jabir al-Jufi opposed them, saying from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit; the correct is the hadith of Abu Ayyub. Al-Thawri narrated it, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub."
"3718","Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit from his father. 3716 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they both said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Usamah ibn al-Had, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"3719","3717 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, they both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Khatmi, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, that he: saw as if he prostrated upon the forehead of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Sit, prostrate, and do as you saw."
"3720","3718 - Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they both said: Sad ibn Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar al-Ansari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated to us, Khuzaymah ibn Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the supplication of the wronged, for it is carried upon the clouds; Allah, Majestic in Might, says: By My might and majesty, I shall surely help you, even after a while."
"3721","3719 - Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Massisi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to man and says: Who created the heavens? He says: Allah. He says: Who created the earth? He says: Allah. Until he says: Who created Allah? When one of you finds that, let him say: I believe in Allah and His messengers."
"3722","3720 - Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Raja al-Abbadani narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, he said: My father held back his weapon on the day of al-Jamal and Siffin; when Ammar was killed, he drew his sword and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The rebellious party shall kill Ammar."
"3723","3721 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abdullah al-Umawi narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his talbiyah, he asked Allah Almighty for His forgiveness and pleasure, and to free him from the Fire."
"3724","3722 - Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abdullah ibn Ikrimah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar."
"3725","3723 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, from Amr ibn Khuzaymah, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about cleaning after relieving oneself. He said: Three stones, among which there is no dung."
"3726","3724 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: Cleaning after relieving oneself was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do not three stones suffice one of you, among which there is no dung? Hisham said: Abu Wajzah informed me, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit. It was said to Sufyan: They say Abu Khuzaymah. He said: No, it is Abu Wajzah the poet."
"3727","3725 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they both said: Abdah ibn Sulayman ibn Urwah informed us, from Amr ibn Khuzaymah, from his father Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In cleaning after relieving oneself, three stones, among which there is no dung."
"3728","3726 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, Amr ibn Khuzaymah informed me, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah, from his father Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about cleaning after relieving oneself. He said: Three stones, among which there is no dung."
"3729","3727 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu Khuzaymah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cleaning after relieving oneself is with three stones, among which there is no dung."
"3730","3728 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh and Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, they both said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, he said: Whoever commits something for which the hadd of that sin is applied upon him, it is its expiation."
"3731","3729 - Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Umarah ibn Khuzaymah, from his father Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever cleans himself with three stones, among which there is no dung, they shall be purification for him."
"3732","3730 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Layth ibn Harun al-Ukli narrated to us, they said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zurarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrated to me, Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrated to me, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a horse from Sawa ibn al-Harith, who denied it; Khuzaymah ibn Thabit testified for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What carried you to testify though you were not present with him? He said: I believed you in what you brought, and I knew you say nothing but truth. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Khuzaymah testifies for, or testifies against, he suffices."
"3733","3731 - Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, that Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to him, that Ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrated to him, from his father Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any servant who commits something Allah forbade, then its hadd is applied upon him, that sin is expiated from him."
"3734","3732 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: Whoever commits a sin and the hadd of that sin is applied upon him, it is its expiation."
"3735","Harami ibn Abdullah al-Khatmi from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit. 3733 - Abu Yazid al-Qaratis narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Harami ibn Abdullah, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be modest, for Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"3736","3734 - Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Abdullah ibn Harami, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, possessor of the two testimonies, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"3737","3735 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Abdullah ibn Harami, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backsides."
"3738","3736 - Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Umar, freedman of Ghufrah, from Abdullah ibn Ali ibn al-Saib, from Ubayd ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Harami, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not shy of the truth; it is not lawful for anyone to approach women in their backs."
"3739","3737 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Umar, freedman of Ghufrah, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ali ibn al-Saib, that he informed him, from Abdullah ibn Husayn ibn Mihsan, from Abdullah ibn Harami, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: I bear witness upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"3740","3738 - Ahmad ibn Rushdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, that Abdullah ibn Ali ibn al-Saib, one of Banu al-Muttalib, narrated to him, that Husayn ibn Mihsan al-Khatmi narrated to him, that Harami ibn Amr al-Khatmi narrated to him, that Khuzaymah ibn Thabit narrated to him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"3741","3739 - Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, they both said: Hassan, freedman of Muhammad ibn Sahl, narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Ali ibn al-Saib, from Harami ibn Abdullah, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"3742","3740 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Kathir informed me, Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Husayn al-Khatmi narrated to me, from Abd al-Malik ibn Qays al-Khatmi, from Harami ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard Khuzaymah ibn Thabit saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backsides."
"3743","3741 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us, (Ha), and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Bundar narrated to us, they both said: Abu Amir narrated to us, Abu Musab al-Madani narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn, from Harami ibn Abdullah al-Waqifi, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, he heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not approach women in their backsides."
"3744","3742 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Husayn, from Harami ibn Abdullah, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backsides."
"3745","3743 - Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Waili, from Harami ibn Abdullah al-Waqifi, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah is not shy of the truth; do not approach women in their backs."
"3746","Amr ibn Uhayhah ibn al-Julah from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit. 3744 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafii al-Makki narrated to us, my uncle Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, he said: I heard my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ali saying: Abdullah ibn Ali ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from Amr ibn Uhayhah ibn al-Julah, he said: I heard Khuzaymah ibn Thabit saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you to approach women in their backs."
"3747","Ibrahim ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit. 3745 - Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibrahim ibn Sad, from Sad ibn Malik, Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, and Usamah ibn Zayd, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This plague is a filth and a remnant of punishment with which a people were punished; when it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not leave it, and when it occurs in it while you are not in it, do not enter it."
"3748","Ata ibn Yasar from Khuzaymah. 3746 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Abd al-Ghaffar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd, Sad ibn Malik, and Khuzaymah ibn Thabit said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This pain is a filth and a remnant of punishment with which a people before you were punished; when it is in a land, do not enter it, and when it is in a land while you are in it, do not approach it, meaning the plague."
"3749","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Khuzaymah. 3747 - Abdan narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Sad narrated to us, my uncle narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding wiping over the khuffs: for the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3750","Abu Ghatfan ibn Tarif al-Murri from Khuzaymah. 3748 - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti and Abu Zayd Ahmad ibn Yazid al-Hawti narrated to us, they both said: Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ghatfan ibn Tarif, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of this herb, let him not approach our mosque."
"3751","Abu Abdullah al-Jadali from Khuzaymah. 3749 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, (Ha), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from his father, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed three days for the traveler, and a day for the resident; by Allah, had the questioner continued in his questioning, he would have made it five."
"3752","3750 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, they both said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said ibn Masruq, from his father, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping over the khuffs. He said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night; had the questioner continued in his questioning, he would have increased him."
"3753","3751 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that a Bedouin asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wiping over the khuffs. He said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night. Had we asked for more, he would have made it five."
"3754","3752 - Said ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wiping over the khuffs for the traveler is three days, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3755","3753 - Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Said ibn Marzuq, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3756","3754 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, they both said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted us in wiping over the khuffs three days and their nights for travelers, and for the resident a day and a night; had we asked for more, he would have increased us."
"3757","3755 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (Ha), and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, (Ha), and Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wipe over the khuffs three days; had we asked for more, he would have increased us."
"3758","3756 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, (Ha), and Said ibn Sayyar al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, they both said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed for the traveler to wipe three, and for the resident a day and a night; had we asked for more, he would have increased us. Abu al-Qasim said: Abu al-Ahwas dropped Amr ibn Maymun from the chain."
"3759","3757 - Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, they both said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed for us to wipe three; had we asked for more, he would have increased us."
"3760","3758 - Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu al-Shatha Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about ablution. He said: Three for the traveler, and a day for the resident, meaning wiping over the khuffs."
"3761","3759 - Khalaf ibn Amr al-Ukbari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The traveler wipes three days. Shubah said: I think he said: and their nights."
"3762","3760 - Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the khuffs, he said: For the traveler three days and their nights."
"3763","3761 - Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, they both said: Dhuad ibn Ulbah narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali al-Akbar, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): regarding wiping over the khuffs, three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3764","3762 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed three days for the traveler, and a day for the resident."
"3765","3763 - Abu Zurah narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, (Ha), and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, (Ha), and Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, (Ha), and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Hammad, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3766","3764 - Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The traveler wipes over the khuffs three days and their nights, and the resident a day and a night."
"3767","3765 - Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (Ha), and Muhammad al-Judhawi al-Qadi narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, (Ha), and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah, from Khuzaymah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the khuffs: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3768","3766 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, (Ha), and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Abu Bilal al-Ashari narrated to us, they both said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3769","3767 - Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Abu Hanifah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah, from Khuzaymah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the khuffs: for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3770","3768 - Ahmad ibn Rustah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl, from Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said regarding wiping over the khuffs: for the traveler three days and their nights."
"3771","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Salih, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding wiping: For the traveler three days, and a day for the resident."
"3772","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu al-Ashath narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Salih, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3773","Abu Zayd al-Hawti narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash al-Himsi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Dhi Himaya, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the two khuffs, he said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3774","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The traveler wipes three days and their nights, and the resident a day and a night."
"3775","Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu Salama al-Kindi narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3776","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Said al-Kindi narrated to us, (h) and Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdillah al-Harawi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3777","Al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Razi narrated to us, and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Bashir narrated to us, Amr ibn Qays narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us with wiping for the resident a day and a night, and for the traveler three."
"3778","Ahmad ibn al-Khadir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abda al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abu Muadh al-Nahwi al-Fadl ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abu Hamza al-Sukkari informed us, from Raqaba ibn Masqala and Ibrahim al-Saigh, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding wiping over the two khuffs, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3779","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding wiping over the two khuffs, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3780","Abdan ibn Ahmad and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram al-Asbahani narrated to us, both said: al-Fadl ibn Sahl al-Araj narrated to us, Khunays ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Wiping over the two khuffs for the traveler is three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3781","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Ashkib narrated to us, Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Dalani narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night, he does not take off."
"3782","Musa ibn Abs al-Himsi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Ufayr ibn Maadan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the two khuffs, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3783","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, and Musa ibn Harun and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Hudba ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wiping over the two khuffs is three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident."
"3784","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abda ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said regarding wiping over the two khuffs, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3785","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, both said: Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymuna narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyya, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3786","Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3787","Al-Husayn ibn al-Samida al-Antaki narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the two khuffs, for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3788","Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari, Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ubayda ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from al-Harith al-Ukli, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Nakhai, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: For the traveler three, and for the resident a day, he wipes over the two khuffs."
"3789","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Mulhami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Yazid ibn al-Walid, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The traveler wipes over his two khuffs three days, and the resident a day and a night."
"3790","Abdillah ibn Najiya narrated to us, Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Zakariyya Abu Yahya al-Buddi narrated to us, Ibrahim al-Nakhai narrated to me, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding wiping over the two khuffs: A day and a night for the resident, and three days and their nights for the traveler."
"3791","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, may Allah have mercy on him, (h) and Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, my father narrated to us, both said: Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hammad and Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the two khuffs: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night. Abdillah said: My father said: This is a mistake. Abu al-Qasim said: Ahmad ibn Hanbal meant that he declared mistaken the hadith of Mansur from Ibrahim from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, and the correct version from the hadith of Mansur is the hadith of Amr ibn Maymun."
"3792","Abu Khalifa narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Arta informed us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3793","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Jawari al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Jazari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sadaqa narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Nakhai, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the two khuffs: For the traveler three days, and for the resident a day and a night."
"3794","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, my uncle Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaida, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Abu Abdillah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night, he wipes over his two khuffs when he has put them on while his feet were pure."
"3795","Shurahbil ibn Sad from Khuzayma ibn Thabit. Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabra narrated to me, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, who said: I heard Khuzayma ibn Thabit saying: There were men among us who, when they came out from relieving themselves, would wash the trace of excrement, so this verse was revealed about them: {In it are men who love to purify themselves}."
"3796","367 - Khuzayma ibn Mamar al-Ansari. Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, both said: Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Khuzayma ibn Mamar al-Ansari, who said: A woman was stoned in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the people said: Her deed has come to nothing. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: It is an expiation for her sins, and she will be gathered apart from that."
"3797","368 - Khuzayma ibn Jaziyy al-Sulami. Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya, from Hibban ibn Jaziyy, from his brother Khuzayma ibn Jaziyy, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, the rabbit? He said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it. I said: And I will not leave it so long as you do not forbid it. He said: It menstruates - or he said: It bleeds. I said: And the hyena? He said: And who eats the hyena?"
"3798","Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Hibban ibn Jaziyy, from his brother Khuzayma ibn Jaziyy, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you to ask you about some things, about the vermin of the earth: What do you say about the lizard? He said: I do not eat it, nor do I declare it unlawful. I said: Then I eat whatever you have not declared unlawful; and why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A community from among the communities was lost, and I saw a creation that made me suspicious. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the rabbit? He said: I do not eat it, nor do I declare it unlawful. He said: Then I eat whatever you have not declared unlawful; and why, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I have been informed that it bleeds. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the hyena? He said: And who eats the hyena? I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the fox? He said: And who eats the fox? I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about the wolf? He said: And does anyone in whom there is good eat the wolf?"
"3799","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq, from Hibban ibn Jaziyy, from Khuzayma ibn Jaziyy, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the vermin of the earth, so he said: Ask about whatever you wish. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me about the lizard? He said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it; I have been told that a community from the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts on the earth. So I said: I will not leave anything you have not forbidden me, that I eat it. He said: I said: And the rabbit? He said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it; I have been informed that it menstruates. So I said: I will not leave anything you have not forbidden, that I eat it. I said: And the fox? He said: Does anyone eat the fox? I said: And the hyena? He said: And does anyone eat the hyena? I said: And the wolf? He said: And does anyone in whom there is good eat the wolf?"
"3800","Chapter: Those whose name is Khalid. 369 - Khalid ibn al-Walid al-Makhzumi, his kunya Abu Sulayman, and he is Khalid ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughira ibn Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Makhzum ibn Yaqaza ibn Murra ibn Kab ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihr ibn Malik, and his mother Lubaba bint al-Harith ibn Hazn ibn Bujayr ibn Ruwayba ibn Abdillah ibn Hilal ibn Amir ibn Sasaa, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him a sword from the swords of Allah. Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wahshi ibn Harb ibn Wahshi narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, directed Khalid ibn al-Walid in fighting the people of apostasy, so he was spoken to about that but he refused to turn him back, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, and he mentioned Khalid ibn al-Walid: What an excellent slave of Allah and brother of the clan, and a sword from the swords of Allah."
"3801","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abdillah ibn Jafar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he announced the death of the people of Muta, said: Then the banner was taken by a sword from the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, so Allah gave victory through him."
"3802","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced the death of the people of Muta upon the minbar, then he said: So the banner was taken by Khalid ibn al-Walid, and he is a sword from the swords of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"3803","Al-Abbas ibn al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, my father narrated to me, (h) and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, Abu Ismail al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Abu Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword from the swords of Allah, mighty and majestic, which Allah has poured upon the disbelievers."
"3804","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiya ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaida narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid said at al-Hira: Nine swords broke in my hand on the day of Muta. He said: There remained in my hands a Yemeni plate of mine."
"3805","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu al-Sukayn Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Amm Abi Zahr ibn Hisn narrated to us, from his grandfather Humayd ibn Munhib, who said: Khuraym ibn Aws said: There was none more hostile to the Arabs than Hurmuz. So when we finished with Musaylima and his companions, we headed toward the side of Basra, and we met Hurmuz at Kazima with a great gathering. Khalid came out to him and called to single combat, so Hurmuz came out to him, and Khalid killed him. And he wrote about that to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, so he gave him as spoils his belongings, the cap of Hurmuz worth one hundred thousand dirhams. And when a man was noble among the Persians, they made a cap worth one hundred thousand dirhams."
"3806","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from his father, that Khalid ibn al-Walid lost a cap of his on the day of Yarmuk, so he said: Search for it, but they did not find it. He said: Search for it, so they found it, and it was a worn-out cap. Khalid said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Umra and shaved his head, so the people rushed to the sides of his hair, and I preceded them to his forelock, so I placed it in this cap, and I did not witness any fighting while it was with me except that I was granted victory."
"3807","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyayna, from Mukhariq ibn Abdillah, who said: I heard Tariq ibn Shihab saying: The cousin of Khalid ibn al-Walid slapped a man from among us, so his uncle disputed with him to Khalid ibn al-Walid. He said: O company of Quraysh, Allah the Exalted has not made for your faces any superiority over our faces except what Allah has favored His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with. Khalid said: Take retaliation. The man said to his nephew: Slap. So when he raised his hand, he said: Leave it for Allah, mighty and majestic."
"3808","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Bishr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Wail, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid wrote to the people of Persia calling them to Islam: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Khalid ibn al-Walid to Rustum and Mihran and the notables of Persia: Peace be upon whoever follows the guidance. As for what follows, we call you to Islam; if you refuse, then give the jizya from your hand while you are humbled. For with me are a people who love killing in the path of Allah as Persia loves wine. And peace be upon whoever follows the guidance."
"3809","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Amir al-Bajali narrated to us, who said: I heard Qays ibn Abi Hazim saying: Khalid ibn al-Walid led the people in prayer wrapped in a garment."
"3810","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Burda, that when Khalid ibn al-Walid came to al-Hira, he said: Bring me the poison. So it was brought to him and he placed it in his palm, then he said: In the name of Allah, and he swallowed it, and it did not harm him."
"3811","Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Said ibn Amr al-Ashathi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I saw Khalid ibn al-Walid brought poison, so he said: What is this? They said: Poison. He said: In the name of Allah, and he swallowed it."
"3812","Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Yahya ibn Husayn, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that there was speech between Khalid ibn al-Walid and Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, so Khalid mentioned from Sad. He said: Stop, for what is between us has not reached our religion."
"3813","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Usama narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaida, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdillah ibn Habib Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, that Khalid ibn al-Walid passed by al-Lat and said: Your disbelief, not your glory; I have seen that Allah has debased you."
"3814","Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Nasr and Hibban ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Abdillah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Abu Wail, who said: When death approached Khalid ibn al-Walid, he said: I sought killing but it was not decreed for me except to die upon my bed. And there is no deed more hopeful than La ilaha illa Allah, and I shield myself with it. Then he said: When I die, look at my weapon and my horse and make them equipment in the path of Allah."
"3815","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Salm ibn Junada narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, who said: They entered upon Khalid ibn al-Walid visiting him in illness, so one of them said: He is in the market. He said: Yes, by Allah, he seeks help through that."
"3816","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr saying: Khalid ibn al-Walid died at Hims in the year twenty-one."
"3817","Ibn Abbas from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought two roasted lizards, and with him was Khalid ibn al-Walid. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined to eat, so it was said: It is lizard, so he withheld his hand. Khalid ibn al-Walid said to him: Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but it is not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it. He said: So Khalid ate while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking at him."
"3818","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, both said: al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Abdillah, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the house of Maymuna bint al-Harith, so a roasted lizard was brought. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined his hand to it, so some of the women who were in the house of Maymuna said: Inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about what he intends to eat from it. They said: It is lizard, so he raised his hand. I said: Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but it was not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it. Khalid said: So I pulled it and ate it while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking."
"3819","Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari informed me, that Abdillah ibn Abbas informed him that Khalid ibn al-Walid, who is called the sword of Allah, informed him, that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and she is his maternal aunt and the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas - so he found with her a roasted lizard brought by her sister Hufayda bint al-Harith from Najd. She presented the lizard to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would rarely extend his hand to food until he was told about it and it was named for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined his hand to the lizard, so a woman from the women present said: Inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what you have presented to him. They said: It is the lizard, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand. Khalid ibn al-Walid said: Do you declare the lizard unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but it was not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it. Khalid said: So I pulled it and ate it while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking, and he did not forbid me."
"3820","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl, from Ibn Abbas, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a roasted lizard, so he inclined his hand to it to eat from it. One of those present said to him: O Messenger of Allah, it is lizard meat. So he raised his hand. Khalid said to him: Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but it was not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it."
"3821","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: Umm Hufayd gifted to Maymuna lizard meat, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and it was presented to him, and he would not eat food until he knew what it was. A woman said: Inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what this is? They said: It is lizard meat gifted by Umm Hufayd to Maymuna. He said: And he intended to eat from it, then he withheld. Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but I find myself disliking it, and it is not from the food of my people. Khalid said: So I ate it while he was sitting, and he did not object to that against me."
"3822","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated to us, Salama ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf informed me, that Abdillah ibn Abbas informed him that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and she is his maternal aunt and the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas - so he found with her a roasted lizard brought by her sister Hufayda bint al-Harith from Najd. She presented the lizard to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would rarely extend his hand to food until he was told about it and it was named for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inclined his hand to the lizard, so a woman from the women present said: Inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what you have presented to him. They said: It is the lizard, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hand. Khalid ibn al-Walid said: Is the lizard unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but it was not in the land of my people, so I find myself disliking it. Khalid said: So I pulled it and ate it while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking, and he did not forbid me."
"3823","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madani narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, who said: My father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Ibn Abbas, that Khalid ibn al-Walid informed him that he entered with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon Maymuna bint al-Harith - and she is his maternal aunt - lizard meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he mentioned the like of it."
"3824","Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Ahmad ibn Khazim, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Maymuna, so she presented to him a lizard cooked with dates. Maymuna said: Inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he eats. When he was informed of it, he withheld his hand from it. They said: Is it unlawful, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, but I dislike it. So Khalid ibn al-Walid pulled it and ate it, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was looking at him."
"3825","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Khalid ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Ibn Abbas, from Khalid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3826","Khalid ibn Hakim ibn Hizam from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Humaydi narrated to us, (h) and Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, al-Qanabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, both said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, Abu Najih narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, who said: Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah seized a man from the people of the land with something, so Khalid ibn al-Walid spoke to him about it. It was said to him: Has the commander become angry? He said: I did not intend to anger him, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are the most severe of them in punishing people in this world."
"3827","Jabir ibn Abdillah from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, my uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For every nation there is a trustee, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah."
"3828","Al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, from his father, from his grandfather, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful to eat the flesh of horses, mules and donkeys."
"3829","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Salama Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, from his father, from his grandfather, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: I fought alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him that the people hastened into their enclosures. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, and I called out among the people: Prayer is assembling, and none enters Paradise except a Muslim. When the people gathered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: What is the matter that the Jews have complained that you hastened into their enclosures? Verily the wealth of the covenanted is not lawful without its right, and forbidden to you are domestic donkeys and their horses, and every fanged beast of prey, and every taloned bird."
"3830","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ubayda narrated to us, who said: I heard Said ibn Ghazwan narrating from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam, from his grandfather, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it: Verily no man reclining upon his couch should say: Whatever we found in the Book of Allah of lawful we deemed lawful, and whatever we found in the Book of Allah of unlawful we deemed unlawful. Verily I forbid to you the wealth of the covenanted, the hadith."
"3831","Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Salih ibn Yahya ibn al-Miqdam, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard Khalid ibn al-Walid saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Khalid, call out among the people: Prayer is assembling; none enters Paradise except a Muslim soul. Then he came out and prayed at midday, then he stood among the people and said: I do not deem lawful the wealth of the covenanted without its right. Perhaps a man among you will say while reclining upon his couch: Whatever we found in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, of lawful we deemed lawful, and whatever we found of unlawful we deemed unlawful. And verily I forbid to you the wealth of the covenanted without its right."
"3832","Malik ibn al-Harith ibn al-Ashtar from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Masud ibn Sad al-Jufi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Shaddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from al-Ashtar, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid used to beat the people for prayer after Asr. Khalid ibn al-Walid said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me in a detachment, so we came upon a household who had professed unity. Ammar said: These have protected themselves from us by their monotheism, but I did not heed the word of Ammar. He said: I shall surely inform the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he complained of me to him. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw he would not retaliate from me, he turned away with his eyes shedding tears. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him back and said: O Khalid, do not revile Ammar, for whoever reviles Ammar, Allah reviles him; and whoever hates Ammar, Allah hates him; and whoever belittles Ammar, Allah belittles him. Khalid said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. By Allah, nothing prevented me from loving him except my belittling him. Khalid said: There is nothing among my sins more fearful to me than my belittling Ammar."
"3833","Abu Muslim al-Kashi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from al-Ashtar, who said: There was speech between Ammar and Khalid ibn al-Walid, so Khalid ibn al-Walid complained of him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shows enmity to Ammar, Allah shows enmity to him; and whoever belittles Ammar, Allah belittles him. Shuba said: Salama said the like of this."
"3834","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, that he heard Abu Yahya saying: Imran ibn Abi al-Jad narrated to me, transmitting from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from al-Ashtar, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid began speaking to us without our asking him, saying: I have not done a deed more fearful to me that it will enter me into the Fire than the affair of Ammar. We said: O Abu Sulayman, what is it? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with some of his Companions to a clan from the Arab clans. I came upon them, and among them was a Muslim household. Ammar spoke to me about some of his companions, saying: Release them. I said: No, until I bring them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if he wishes he releases them, and if he wishes he does with them what he wants. I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ammar sought permission and entered, saying: O Messenger of Allah, have you not seen what Khalid did and did? Khalid said: By Allah, were it not for your sitting, Ibn Sumayya would not have reviled me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go out, O Ammar. So he went out weeping, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not support me against Khalid. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Why did you not answer the man? I said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing prevented me from him except my disdain for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever disdains Ammar, Allah disdains him; and whoever reviles Ammar, Allah reviles him; and whoever disparages Ammar, Allah disparages him. So I went out and followed him and spoke to him until he sought forgiveness for me."
"3835","Ubayd ibn Kathir al-Tammar al-Kufi narrated to us, Awn ibn Sallam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Imran ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from al-Ashtar, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid began speaking to us without our asking him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a clan from the Arab clans, then he mentioned the like of it."
"3836","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Harithi narrated to us, Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from his uncle Makhrama ibn Rabia, from al-Ashtar, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid narrated to me, saying: Ammar reviled me in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, were it not for you, Ibn Sumayya would not have reviled me. He said: Gently, O Khalid; whoever reviles Ammar, Allah reviles him; and whoever disdains Ammar, Allah disdains him."
"3837","Alqama ibn Qays from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Alqama ibn Qays, who said: I came to Sham and met Khalid ibn al-Walid, may Allah be pleased with him, and I heard him narrating, saying: There was between me and Ammar ibn Yasir some of what occurs between people. I came forward and rebuked him harshly, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of me to him. When I saw him complaining of me, I also came forward against him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, do you not see what he is saying while you are present? He said: Gently, O Khalid, say nothing but good, for whoever hates Ammar, Allah hates him; and whoever shows enmity to him, Allah shows enmity to him. When I heard that, I kept seeking out Ammar until I met him, so I apologized to him and asked whatever was in his heart against me."
"3838","Qays ibn Abi Hazim from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Umayr ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Miqlas narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to some people of Khatham, so they sought protection by prostration, but he killed them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid their blood-money at half, then he said: I am free from every Muslim who resides among the polytheists; their two fires should not be visible to each other."
"3839","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Mihran narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: I saw Khalid ibn al-Walid on the day of Yarmuk shooting between two targets, and with him were men from the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And he said: We were commanded to teach our children shooting and the Quran."
"3840","Abu al-Aliya from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Mamari narrated to us, al-Musayyib ibn Wadih narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from Abu al-Aliya, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I find fright at night. He said: Shall I not teach you words taught to me by Jibril, peace be upon him, and he claimed that a demon from the jinn plots against me. He said: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which no righteous nor wicked transcends, from the evil of what descends from the sky and what ascends therein, and from the evil of what He spread in the earth and what comes out of it, and from the evil of the trials of night and the trials of day, and from the evil of the knockers of night and day, except a knocker that knocks with good, O Most Merciful."
"3841","Ibn Sabit from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Misar, from Ibn Sabit, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, who said: I used to lie awake at night, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not teach you words which, when you say them, you sleep? Say: O Allah, Lord of the heavens and what they shade, and Lord of the earths and what they carry, and Lord of the devils and what they mislead, be to me a protector from the evil of all jinn and men, and that any of them should transgress against me or harm me. Mighty is Your protection, glorified is Your praise, and there is no god but You."
"3842","Abu Abdillah al-Ashari from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Abu Amir Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shayba ibn al-Ahnaf narrated to me, from Abu Sallam al-Aswad, from Abu Salih al-Ashari, from Abu Abdillah al-Ashari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man not completing his bowing, pecking in his prostration while praying. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this one died upon this state of his, he would die upon other than the religion of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who does not complete his bowing and pecks in his prostration is like the hungry one who eats one date and two dates; they do not avail him anything. Abu Salih said: I said to Abu Abdillah: Who narrated this to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: The commanders of the armies, Amr ibn al-As and Khalid ibn al-Walid, and Shurahbil ibn Hasana heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3843","Azra ibn Qays from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn Musawir al-Jawhari narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, (h) and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, both said: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salama, from Azra ibn Qays, who said: Khalid ibn al-Walid said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, the Commander of the Faithful, may Allah be pleased with him, wrote to me when Sham had laid down its provisions of wheat and honey, and he ordered me to march to Hind. He said: And Hind in our view that day was Basra, and I was averse to that. He said: So a man stood and said: O Abu Sulayman, fear Allah, mighty and majestic, for trials have appeared. He said: While Ibn al-Khattab is alive? It will only be after him, while the people are at Dhi Billiyan, and Dhi Billiyan is at such-and-such place. A man looks and reflects whether he can find a place untouched by the like of what befell his place of trial and evil, and he does not find it. He said: And those are the days which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned before the Hour, the days of killing. So we seek refuge in Allah lest those days reach us and you."
"3844","Al-Mughira Abu al-Yasa from Khalid ibn al-Walid. Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Abdillah al-Umawi narrated to us, al-Yasa ibn al-Mughira narrated to me, from his father, from Khalid ibn al-Walid, that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of straitness in his dwelling, so he said: Raise to the sky and ask Allah for spaciousness."
"3845","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Yasa ibn al-Mughira, from Khalid ibn al-Walid the like of it."
"3846","Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Kulayb Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, a Badri. Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr saying: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari is Khalid ibn Zayd."
"3847","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu Thalaba ibn Abd Awf ibn Ghanm, Abu Ayyub, and his name is Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Kulayb ibn Thalaba."
"3848","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said narrated to us, Hayyaj ibn Bistam narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ward, from Abu Muhammad, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with me, and I was the first upon whom he stayed."
"3849","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Zibyan, who said: Abu Ayyub raided the Romans and fell ill. When his death approached, he said: When I die, carry me, and when you face the enemy, carry me beneath your feet."
"3850","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr saying: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari died in the land of the Romans in the time of Muawiya."
"3851","Al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Ibn Shihab, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Abu Ayyub Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Kulayb from Banu al-Najjar."
"3852","Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakkai narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, in naming those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar, then from Banu al-Khazraj, then from Banu al-Najjar: Abu Ayyub Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Kulayb ibn Thalaba ibn Abd Awf ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar, and he died at Constantinople with Yazid ibn Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan in the year fifty-one."
"3853","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Madini Fustuqa narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Adi, who said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari perished in the year fifty in the land of the Romans while raiding with Yazid."
"3854","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: Abu Ayyub came to Muawiya, may Allah have mercy on them both, and complained to him that he had a debt upon him, then he mentioned the hadith."
"3855","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdillah, who said: I married in the time of my father, so my father invited the people, and Abu Ayyub was among those we invited, and they had covered my house with a green striped cloak. Abu Ayyub came forward and entered, and he saw me standing. He looked and saw the house covered with a green striped cloak, so he said: O Abdillah, do you cover the walls? My father said, feeling shy: The women overcame us, O Abu Ayyub. He said: Whoever fears being overcome by women, I did not fear that you would be overcome. Then he said: I will not eat food for you nor enter a house for you. Then he went out, may Allah have mercy on him."
"3856","Abu Umama al-Bahili from Abu Ayyub. Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydillah ibn Zahr, from Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umama, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with me a month. I saw him that when the sun declined or set, or as he said, if he was in some worldly work he cast it aside, and if he was sleeping it was as if awakened. So he would stand and wash or perform ablution, then pray four rakats, completing them and perfecting them and being unhurried in them. When he intended to depart, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have seen you that when the sun declines or sets, if in your hand is some worldly work you cast it aside, or you were sleeping as if awakened, then you wash or perform ablution, then pray four rakats, completing them and being unhurried in them and perfecting them? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The doors of heaven, or the doors of Paradise, are opened at that hour, so none meets it with this prayer, and I loved that there should ascend from me to my Lord in that hour goodness."
"3857","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Ali al-Naqid al-Basri narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Marthad ibn Abdillah al-Yazani, from Abu Umama, from Abu Ayyub, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with me, I said: May my father and mother be ransom for you, I dislike being above you while you are below me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be gentle with us that we be in the lower part, for those who visit us from the people. I saw a jar of ours break and its water spill, so I stood, I and Umm Ayyub, with a velvet cloth of ours - we had no blanket besides it - drying the water with it, fearing that something of it would reach the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and harm him. We would prepare food, and when he returned what remained of it, we sought out the places of his fingers and ate from them, intending thereby blessing. He returned to us his supper one night, and we had put in it garlic or onion, and we did not see in it the trace of his fingers. I mentioned to him what we used to do and what we saw of his returning the food without eating, so he said: I found in it the smell of this tree, and I am a man who converses privately, so I did not love that its smell be found from me. As for you, then eat it."
"3858","Al-Bara ibn Azib from Abu Ayyub. Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, both said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shuba informed us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a voice at sunset, or at the setting of the sun, and said: These are the Jews being punished in their graves."
"3859","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam Abu Said al-Muallim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ayyash al-Shibami narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when the sun set or yellowed toward setting, and with me was a small vessel of water. The Messenger of Allah went for his need, and I sat waiting for him until he came, so I performed ablution for him. He said: O Abu Ayyub, do you hear what I hear? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: I hear the voices of the Jews being punished in their graves."
"3860","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Thumama ibn Abdillah ibn Anas, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a child was buried, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If anyone were to escape the squeeze of the grave, this child would have escaped it."
"3861","Al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib from Abu Ayyub. Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, (h) and Khayr ibn Arafa al-Misri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi al-Jurjusi al-Himsi narrated to us, (h) and Ismail ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najda al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, both of them, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Measure your food, it will be blessed for you therein."
"3862","Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani from Abu Ayyub. Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar and Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, both said: Umayya ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Said ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from Abu Ayyub, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"3863","Anas ibn Malik from Abu Ayyub. Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, came, and the Ansar were slow in meeting him, and he did nothing to them. Abu Ayyub said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Selfishness will befall you, so be patient until you meet me. Muawiya said: Then be patient. Abu Ayyub said: We are patient as we were commanded, and by Allah we shall not dispute it with you."
"3864","Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi from Abu Ayyub. Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, from Khallad ibn Yahya, Misar narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed them both at Jam, Maghrib and Isha combined."
"3865","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Mutarrif ibn Abdillah narrated to us, (h) and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, (h) and Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, (h) and Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-Sanani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, all of them from Malik ibn Anas, from Yahya ibn Said, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who informed him that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifa together. And the wording is for the hadith of Mutarrif."
"3866","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I prayed Maghrib and Isha with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage at Muzdalifa."
"3867","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said informed me, Adi ibn Thabit informed me, that Abdillah ibn Yazid narrated to him that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari informed him that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Pilgrimage Maghrib and the latter Isha at Muzdalifa."
"3868","Musa ibn Harun and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Jam, and he combined between Maghrib and Isha."
"3869","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruwasi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like of it."
"3870","Idris ibn Jafar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, (h) and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3871","Abu Muslim al-Kashi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb and Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, both said: Shuba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined between Maghrib and Isha at Jam."
"3872","Fudayl ibn Muhammad al-Malati narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Jabir, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at Jam Maghrib three, and Isha two rakats with a single iqama."
"3873","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba and Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifa with a single iqama."
"3874","Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Judhuyi al-Qadi narrated to us, Uqba ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plundering and mutilation."
"3875","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Shurahbil al-Qurashi, that Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi narrated to him from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; and whoever among your women believes in Allah and the Last Day, let them not enter the bathhouse."
"3876","Jabir ibn Samura from Abu Ayyub. Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samura, from Abu Ayyub, who said: When food was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would take from it, then send it to us. We were brought food from which he had not taken anything, so I said to the woman: Do not hasten. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: This greenery, and I dislike its smell. Abu Ayyub said: Then I dislike what you disliked therein, O Messenger of Allah."
"3877","Abdillah ibn Umar from Abu Ayyub. Abdillah ibn Zaydan al-Bajali al-Kufi narrated to us, Hamza ibn Awn al-Masudi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Umar ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I never prayed behind your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that I heard him, when he finished his prayer, saying: O Allah, forgive me my errors and all my sins; O Allah, revive me and mend me and provide for me and guide me to righteous deeds and manners; none guides to their righteousness nor turns away their evil except You."
"3878","Ibn Abbas from Abu Ayyub. Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Firdaws ibn al-Ashari narrated to us, Masud ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, that Abu Ayyub ibn Zayd al-Ansari, with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed when he migrated to Madina, raided the land of the Romans and passed by Muawiya, may Allah be pleased with him, who treated him coldly. He went on, then returned from his raid and passed by him, and he treated him coldly and paid him no attention. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that we would see after him selfishness. Muawiya said: Then what did he command you? He said: He commanded us to be patient. He said: Then be patient. He came to Abdillah ibn Abbas at Basra, whom Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, had appointed over it, and said: O Abu Ayyub, I want to vacate my dwelling for you as you vacated for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He ordered his family so they went out, and he gave him everything over which he closed the door. When it was his departure, he said: Your need? He said: My need is my stipend and eight slaves to work on my land. His stipend was four thousand, so he multiplied it for him five times, giving him twenty thousand and forty slaves."
"3879","Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas the like of it."
"3880","Abu Ruhm al-Samai from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Abu al-Khayr, from Abu Ruhm al-Samai, that Abu Ayyub narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed in his lower house, while I was in the upper chamber. Water spilled in the upper chamber, so I stood, I and Umm Ayyub, with a velvet cloth of ours following the water, out of concern lest it reach the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I came down to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while anxious, saying: O Messenger of Allah, it is not fitting that we be above you; move to the upper chamber. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his belongings moved, and his belongings were little. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you used to send us food and I would look in it; when I saw the trace of your fingers, I placed my hand in it, until this food which you sent to me, I looked in it and did not see the trace of your fingers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, in it is onion, and I disliked eating it because of the angel who comes to me. As for you, then eat it."
"3881","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Ala Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Damdam ibn Zura, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Ruhm al-Samai, that he used to narrate, that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Every prayer removes the sin before it."
"3882","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Humayd informed us, Abu Muayd Hafs ibn Ghaylan informed me, who said: I heard Makhul narrating from Abu Ruhm al-Samai, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer removes the sin before it."
"3883","Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Abu Ruhm, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prayer removes the sin before it."
"3884","Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zuba narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, who said: I heard Abu Ruhm, that he heard Abbad ibn Nashira saying: I heard Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to them and said: My Lord, mighty and majestic, gave me choice between seventy thousand entering Paradise pardoned without reckoning, and the handful with Him. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, will your Lord handful for you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, then came out to them while magnifying, saying: My Lord, mighty and majestic, increased me: with every thousand seventy thousand, and the handful with Him. Abu Ruhm said: O Abu Ayyub, what do you think the handful of Allah is? The people consumed it with their mouths. Abu Ayyub said: Leave your companion; I shall inform you of the handful of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as I think, rather as one certain: The handful of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is that he says: My Lord, whoever testifies that there is no god but You alone without partner, and that Muhammad is Your slave and Messenger, then his heart confirms his tongue, Paradise becomes due for him."
"3885","Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, (h) and Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi and al-Haytham ibn Kharija narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Amr, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu Ruhm al-Samai, from Abu al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise, He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things capable, ten times, there is written for him for every one he says ten good deeds, and Allah raises him thereby ten degrees, and they are for him as freeing ten necks, and they are for him a guard from the beginning of the day to its end, and he does not do on that day a deed that overcomes them; and if he says them in the evening, the like of that."
"3886","Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, both said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Rabia ibn Mutayr, from Abu Ruhm al-Jurhumi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable, in the morning ten times, Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, and they are for him equal to ten necks, and he is protected from Satan; and whoever says them in the evening, the like of that."
"3887","Abu Zura Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, (h) and Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, both said: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, Abu Ruhm al-Samai narrated to us, that Abu Ayyub narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none who does not associate anything with Allah, establishes prayer, gives zakat, fasts Ramadan, and avoids the major sins, except that Paradise becomes due for him. They asked him: What are the major sins? He said: Associating with Allah, killing the Muslim soul, and fleeing on the day of battle."
"3888","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Damdam ibn Zura, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, who said: Abu Ruhm used to narrate, that Abu Ayyub narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: Whoever comes to Allah worshipping Him, associating nothing with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakat, fasts Ramadan, and avoids the major sins, then for him is Paradise. They asked him: And what are the major sins? He said: Associating with Allah, killing the Muslim soul, and fleeing on the day of battle."
"3889","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq narrated to us, Maslama ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Makhul, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salama, from Abu Ruhm al-Samai, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer, when taken, is met by the merciful from among the servants of Allah as you meet the bearer of glad tidings in this world. They say: Look to your companion to rest, for he was in severe distress. Then they ask him: What did so-and-so do? And what did so-and-so do? Has she married? When they ask him about a man who died before him, he says: Alas, he died before me. They say: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; he was taken to his mother Hawiya, an evil mother and an evil nurturer. He said: Your deeds are presented to your relatives and kin from the people of the Hereafter. If it is good, they rejoice and are glad, saying: O Allah, this is Your bounty and mercy, so complete Your favor upon him and cause him to die upon it. And the deed of the evildoer is presented to them, so they say: O Allah, inspire him a righteous deed with which You are pleased with him and bring him near to You."
"3890","Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami narrated to us, Maslama ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid and Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Makhul, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Salama, from Abu Ruhm al-Samai, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3891","Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Damdam ibn Zura narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salama used to narrate, that Abu Ruhm narrated to them, that Abu Ayyub narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The soul of the believer, when he dies, is met by the merciful from among the servants of Allah as they meet the bearer of glad tidings in this world. They say: Look to your companion to rest, for he was in severe distress. Then they ask him: What did so-and-so do? What did so-and-so do? Has she married? When they ask him about one who died before him, he says: Alas, he died before me. They say: To Allah we belong and to Him we return; he was taken to his mother Hawiya, an evil mother and an evil nurturer."
"3892","Said ibn al-Musayyib from Abu Ayyub. Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Ayyub, that he took something from the Prophet and said: May evil not be with you, O Abu Ayyub."
"3893","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Fudayl al-Rasibi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined between Maghrib and Isha prayers at Muzdalifa with one adhan and one iqama."
"3894","Urwa ibn al-Zubayr from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him. Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Uqba ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the two rakats of Maghrib Surah al-Anfal."
"3895","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, or Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited in Maghrib al-Araf."
"3896","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Muqad narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Water is from water."
"3897","Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Ayyub. Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abdillah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No prophet was sent, nor was there after him a caliph, except that he had two confidants: a confidant commanding him with good and forbidding him evil, and a confidant not sparing him corruption. Whoever is protected from the evil confidant has been protected."
"3898","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Hafs narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi al-Uqayli, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, here are a people who recite loudly in the daytime prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Why do you not pelt them with dung."
"3899","Salim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar from Abu Ayyub. Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahfuz ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated to us, Amr ibn Shimr narrated to us, from Jabir, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abdillah and Aban ibn Hasan mentioning that Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought a man who had committed immorality with a boy of Quraysh of known lineage. Uthman said: Woe to you, where are the witnesses? Is he married? They said: He has married a woman but has not yet consummated with her. Ali said to Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both: Had he consummated with her, stoning would be due upon him; as for since he has not consummated with his wife, flog him the hadd. Abu Ayyub said: I testify that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying that which Abu al-Hasan mentioned. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, ordered concerning him, so he was flogged one hundred."
"3900","Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywa ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Abu Sakhr narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abu Sakhr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar, Abu Ayyub narrated to me, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: On the night I was taken, I passed by Ibrahim, peace be upon him. He said: O Jibril, who is this with you? He said: Muhammad. He greeted me and welcomed me, saying: Command your nation to increase the planting of Paradise, for its soil is good and spacious. I said: And what is the planting of Paradise? He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"3901","Abdillah ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas from Abu Ayyub. Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, both said: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Yunus ibn Humran informed me, from Kharija ibn Abdillah ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from his father, who said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said to me: Shall I not teach you a word taught to me by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes, O uncle. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stayed with me, said: Shall I not teach you, O Abu Ayyub, a word from the treasure of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransom for you. He said: Increase saying: There is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"3902","Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas from Abu Ayyub. Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and al-Hasan ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, both said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to me, al-Muttalib ibn Abdillah ibn Hantab narrated to me, from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: I met Abu Ayyub, and he said to me: Shall I not command you with what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me? To increase saying: There is no power nor strength except through Allah, for it is from the treasures of Paradise."
"3903","Khalid ibn Abi Ayyub from his father, may Allah be pleased with him. Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Nafi al-Tahhan al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Haywa ibn Shurayh informed me, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, that Ayyub ibn Khalid ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to him from his father, from his grandfather Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Conceal the sin, then perform ablution and perfect the ablution, then pray what Allah has written for you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: O Allah, You decree and I do not decree, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You see for me in so-and-so - name her by her name - good in my worldly life and my Hereafter, then decree her for me - or he said: - then ordain her for me."
"3904","Umar ibn Thabit al-Ansari from Abu Ayyub. Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj and Dawud ibn Qays and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sabra, all of them from Sad ibn Abi Said, brother of Yahya ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj from Banu al-Khazraj, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, that is the fasting of eternity. He said: I said to him: Every day ten? He said: Yes."
"3905","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, may Allah have mercy on him, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Warqa, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, it is the fasting of eternity."
"3906","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, (h) and Ibrahim ibn Naila al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, (h) and Abu Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six days from Shawwal has fasted the year."
"3907","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, (h) and Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Musa narrated to us, both said: al-Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal is as one who fasted eternity."
"3908","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, (h) and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, both said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal has fasted eternity."
"3909","Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Baghdadi and Ubaydillah ibn Muhammad ibn Shabib al-Basri narrated to us, both said: al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Jazari narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six from Shawwal has fasted eternity."
"3910","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Qurra ibn Abd al-Rahman and Amr ibn al-Harith and Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd informed me, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan then follows it with six from Shawwal is as the fasting of eternity."
"3911","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts Ramadan then follows it from Shawwal has fasted eternity."
"3912","Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Qurra ibn Abd al-Rahman and Amr ibn al-Harith and Muhammad ibn Humayd and al-Qasim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar informed me, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and six from Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the year."
"3913","Al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, (h) and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Dirar ibn Surad narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sad ibn Said and Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, it is as if he fasted eternity."
"3914","Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Usayd al-Asbahani and al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya al-Mutarriz narrated to us, both said: Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, it is as if he fasted eternity. Hafs said: Then I met Sad and he narrated to me."
"3915","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Kamil ibn Talha al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ibn Lahia narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Said, from his brother Yahya ibn Said, Umar ibn Thabit narrated to me, who said: I heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six, it is as if he fasted the whole year."
"3916","Ishaq ibn Abi Hassan al-Anmati narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Hakim al-Hudhali, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, that is like fasting the lifetime."
"3917","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from Yahya ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, that is like fasting the lifetime."
"3918","Abd al-Rahman Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Sad ibn Said, from Yahya ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six from Shawwal, that is the fast of a year."
"3919","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim Abu Yahya Saiqah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it for stool or urine; face east or west."
"3920","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Yusuf ibn Himas, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Ayyub, that he found some boys who had driven a fox into a corner, so he drove them away, and I only know that he said: Is this done in the sanctuary of Allah?"
"3921","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Umarah ibn Sayyad, that Ata ibn Yasar informed him, that Abu Ayyub al-Ansari informed him, who said: We used to sacrifice one sheep, a man slaughtering it for himself and his household, then people boasted afterwards and it became boasting."
"3922","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us (h), and Mahmud ibn Ali al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Umarah ibn Abdullah ibn Sayyad, from Ata ibn Yasar, who said: I asked Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), how were the sacrifices among you in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: A man in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sacrifice a sheep for himself and his household, so they would eat and feed from it, then people boasted and it became as you see."
"3923","Abu al-Zinba Ruh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us (h), and Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Muqri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wasiti narrated to us (h), and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to me, they said: Ibrahim ibn Sad al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to face the qiblah with stool or urine, then when we came to Syria we found their toilets built facing the qiblah, so we turn aside and seek Allah's forgiveness."
"3924","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Ubadah ibn Umayr ibn Ubadah ibn Awf who said: Abu Ayyub said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Ayyub, shall I not guide you to a charity beloved to Allah and His Messenger? You reconcile between people when they hate one another and are corrupt."
"3925","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us (h), and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they both said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Zuhri, from Hakim ibn Bashir, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is charity given to a hostile relative."
"3926","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, who said: I heard Musa ibn Talhah mention from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that a Bedouin met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his journey and said: Inform me of what brings me near to Paradise and distances me from the Fire? He said: You worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, and join ties of kinship."
"3927","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Tell me of a deed that admits me to Paradise. The people said: What is with him, what is with him? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has a need, what is with him. You worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, and join ties of kinship; leave it from you."
"3928","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Mundhir al-Qazzaz and Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Guide me to a deed that brings me near to Paradise and distances me from the Fire. He said: You worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, establish prayer, give zakat, and join ties of kinship. The man turned away, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he holds fast to what he was commanded, he will enter Paradise."
"3929","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Malik al-Ashjai informed us, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Muzaynah, Juhaynah, Ashja, Aslam, Ghifar, and whoever was of Banu Kab are allies apart from people, and Allah and His Messenger are their allies."
"3930","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us (h), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they both said: Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abi Farwah, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Qari, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Perform ablution for touching the penis, and perhaps he said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"3931","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Jadah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Qari, who says: Abu Ayyub informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution when he ate what fire had changed."
"3932","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, one who heard Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Qari informed me, who says: Abu Ayyub informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution for what fire has touched."
"3933","al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Rafi ibn Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu Ayyub in Egypt say: By Allah, I do not know what to do with these linens, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to stool or urine, let him not face the qiblah with his private part."
"3934","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, from Rafi ibn Ishaq, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah with your private parts, nor turn your backs to it."
"3935","Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi al-Basri narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yaqub, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah Abu Talhah, from Rafi ibn Ishaq, a man of the early people of Madinah, that he heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to face the qiblah or turn our backs to it when one of us goes to urinate or defecate."
"3936","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Talhah narrated to me, a man of us narrated to me, who said: I heard Abu Ayyub, upon whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you urinates or defecates, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it with his private part."
"3937","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the place of relieving, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, but face east or west."
"3938","Abu Bakr ibn Sadaqah and Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, they said: al-Haytham ibn Marwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it for stool or urine, and face east or west."
"3939","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi and Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us (h), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it for urine or stool, but face east or west."
"3940","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you goes to the place of relieving, let him not face the qiblah nor give it his back; face east or west."
"3941","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Shahin narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah with stool or urine, but face east or west."
"3942","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Musafir narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade one who goes to relieve himself to face the qiblah, and said: Face east or west."
"3943","Ahmad ibn Tahir ibn Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to me, Idris ibn Yahya al-Khawlani narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you goes out for relieving, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, but face east or west."
"3944","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz narrated to me, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah said: Whoever of you goes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah nor give it his back; face east or west."
"3945","Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, from Qurrah, Yunus and Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, Ata ibn Yazid narrated to me, that he heard Abu Ayyub say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade one who intends relieving to face the qiblah, and said: Face east and west."
"3946","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, Ata ibn Yazid narrated to us, that he heard Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), forbid one who goes to relieve himself to face the qiblah, and he said: Face east or west. He did not raise it."
"3947","Aslam ibn Sahl al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah nor turn his back to it, but face east and west."
"3948","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah nor turn your backs to it, but face east and west."
"3949","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not face the qiblah with urine or stool, but face east or west."
"3950","Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu Marwan al-Uthmani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade one who goes to relieve himself to face the qiblah, and said: Face east or west."
"3951","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, I only know that he raised it, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3952","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"3953","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3954","Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, conveying it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3955","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us (h), and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us (h), and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3956","Abu Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Abi Mani al-Rusafi narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to abandon his brother for more than three nights; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3957","Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Jundai, that Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3958","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Yunus informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3959","Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, who said: I read to Anas ibn Iyad, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not turn your backs on one another and do not sever ties, and be servants of Allah as brothers; the abandonment of the believers is three, and if they speak, otherwise Allah turns away from them until they speak."
"3960","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Muadh narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us (h), and Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, all of them from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three nights; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3961","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated to us, from his uncle, who said: Ata ibn Yazid narrated to me, that Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim man to abandon his brother for more than three nights; they meet, and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3962","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uzayz al-Ayli narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, Ata ibn Yazid informed me that he heard Ubayy ibn Kab say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days; this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of them is the one who begins with greeting."
"3963","Abu Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdullah al-Bablutti narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, Ata narrated to me, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is a right; whoever wishes may pray witr with five, whoever wishes may pray witr with three, and whoever wishes may pray witr with one."
"3964","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Quraysh ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is a right; whoever loves to pray witr with five, let him do so, whoever loves to pray witr with three, let him do so, and whoever loves to pray witr with one, let him do so."
"3965","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Marwazi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is five or three or one, and if you cannot, then gesture with a gesture. The wording is of the hadith of Ibn Sulayman."
"3966","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatrani narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, raising it, who said: Witr is obligatory on every Muslim; whoever can pray witr with five, let him do so, whoever cannot pray with five, let him pray with three, whoever cannot pray with three, let him pray with one, and whoever cannot pray with one, let him gesture with a gesture."
"3967","Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Dubarah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Sulayk narrated to me, Duwayd ibn Nafi informed me, Ibn Shihab informed me, Ata ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is a right; whoever wishes may pray witr with seven, whoever wishes with five, whoever wishes with three, and whoever wishes with one."
"3968","Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Shafii narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, conveying it, who said: Witr is a right; whoever wishes may pray witr with seven, whoever wishes with five, whoever wishes with three, and whoever wishes with one."
"3969","al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Yasir narrated to us, Qatan ibn Ibrahim al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah, from Abu Hafsah, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is a right; whoever wishes may pray witr with five, whoever wishes with three, whoever wishes with one, and whoever is overcome, let him gesture with a gesture."
"3970","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us (h), and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Karabisi narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Laythi narrated to us, who said: I heard Ibn Shihab say: I testify that Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi narrated to me, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever plants a planting, Allah writes for him reward according to what comes out of the fruit of that planting."
"3971","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Harun ibn Abdullah al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Aziz Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Laythi narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to dispute on the Day of Resurrection are a man and his wife; by Allah, her tongue will not speak, but her hands and feet will testify against her for what she concealed from her husband, and his hands and feet will testify for what he bestowed on her. Then a man and his household will be called, and likewise. Then the people of the markets will be called, and there will be no small coins nor carats there, but the good deeds of this one will be given to this one who was wronged, and the evil deeds of this one who wronged him. Then the tyrants will be brought in shackles of iron, and it will be said: Bring them to the Fire. By Allah, I do not know whether they will enter it, or as Allah Almighty said: There is none of you but will come to it, a decree from your Lord, inevitable. Then We will save those who feared Allah and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees."
"3972","Abu Aqil Anas ibn Salm al-Khawlani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Raja al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Zubaydi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two men may head to the mosque and one returns with prayer better than the other if he is better in intellect, while the other returns with prayer not equal to an atom's weight."
"3973","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Muslims, whoever of you comes to Friday, let him wash, and if he finds perfume it is no harm to touch some, and upon you is this siwak. Ata ibn Yazid said: Ibn Abbas, who narrated to me what Abu Ayyub narrated to me, said, Abdullah said: As for washing, yes, and as for perfume, I do not know."
"3974","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Azraqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ata ibn Yazid narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no Monday or Thursday but deeds are raised therein except the deeds of two who abandon one another."
"3975","Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Azraqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ata ibn Yazid narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Those who love one another for Allah are on chairs of ruby around the Throne."
"3976","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated to us, Asim ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Laythi narrated to me, who said: I heard Sulayman ibn Ata ibn Yazid narrate from his father, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sever ties nor turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers; the abandonment of the believers is three, and if they do not speak, Allah turns away from them until they speak."
"3977","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah."
"3978","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Qanabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, that Ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah differed at al-Abwa; Ibn Abbas said: One in ihram washes his head, and al-Miswar said: One in ihram does not wash his head. Ibn Abbas sent him to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari and found him washing between the two posts, screening himself with a garment. He said: I greeted him, and he said: Who is this? I said: I am Abdullah ibn Hunayn; Abdullah ibn Abbas sent me to you asking you how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wash his head while in ihram? So Abu Ayyub placed his hand on the garment and lowered me, then said to a man pouring over him: Pour. He poured over his head, then moved his head with his hands, bringing them forward and back, then said: Thus I saw him do."
"3979","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us (h), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, from his father, who said: Ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah disputed about one in ihram washing his head, so they sent me to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. I came to him while he washed between the two sides of a well; when he saw me he drew the garment to himself. I said: Your nephew Ibn Abbas sent me to you asking you how you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pour water over his head while in ihram? He poured water over his head and said: Thus, and he said with his hand over his head, bringing forward and back, three times."
"3980","al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn, that Abdullah ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah differed about one in ihram washing his head with water without impurity, so they sent me to Abu Ayyub while he was at some waters of Makkah asking him about that. I came to him and found Abu Ayyub between the two posts washing his head, screened by a garment. I asked him, so he lowered the garment with his hand until his head appeared, then moved his head and hair with his hands, bringing his hands forward in his hair and back, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wash while in ihram. Ibrahim said: I returned to them and informed them."
"3981","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Hunayn narrated to me, from his father, who said: I was with Ibn Abbas and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah at al-Abwa, and we talked until they mentioned one in ihram washing his head. Al-Miswar said: No, and Ibn Abbas said: Yes. Ibn Abbas sent me to Abu Ayyub, conveying: Your nephew Abdullah ibn Abbas greets you and asks you: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wash and wash his head when in ihram? I found him washing between the two sides of a well, screened by a garment. When I named myself to him and asked him, he drew the garment to himself until his face and head appeared to me, while a man stood at the well pouring water over him. Abu Ayyub passed his hands over his head, bringing them forward and back. Al-Miswar said to Ibn Abbas: I will never dispute with you again. Ibn Jurayj did not raise it."
"3982","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from al-Rabi ibn Malik, from Ibn Hunayn, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wash his head while in ihram."
"3983","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Umarah ibn Abdullah ibn Sayyad, from Abu Ayyub, who said: We performed Umrah with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a household sacrificing a sheep, then a man sacrificed two sheep, and afterwards it was boasting."
"3984","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us (h), and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us (h), and Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Hushaym narrated to us, Mansur ibn Zadham informed us, from Ibn Sirin, from Aflah, the freedman of Abu Ayyub, from Abu Ayyub that he used to command wiping over the two leather socks yet wash his feet. It was said to him about that, so he said: Evil is my wealth if its benefit is for you and its sin upon me; I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over the leather socks and command it, but ablution is beloved to me."
"3985","Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, al-Musayyab ibn Wadih narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Shuayb narrate from Ibn Sirin, Aflah, the servant of Abu Ayyub, narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over the leather socks and the cap."
"3986","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Thabit ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Aflah, the freedman of Abu Ayyub, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with him; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed below and Abu Ayyub above. Abu Ayyub woke one night and said: Do we walk above the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He came down to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: The lower is gentler for us. Abu Ayyub, when he sent food to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would ask about the places of the traces of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Ayyub sent him food containing garlic, and did not see therein the trace of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is it forbidden? He said: No, but I dislike it. He said: I dislike what you disliked, or what you dislike. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be visited."
"3987","Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ashjai narrated to us, Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah narrated to us, from Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh, from Aflah, the freedman of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he passed by Zayd ibn Thabit and Abu Ayyub while they sat at the mosque of funerals. One of them said to his companion: Do you remember our hadith the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us in this gathering we are in? He said: Yes, about Madinah; I heard him claim that a time will come upon people in which conquests of the earth will be opened, and men will go out to them attaining ease, life and food, then pass by brothers of theirs, pilgrims or performers of Umrah, saying: What keeps you in hardship of life and severity of hunger? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One going and one staying - until he said it repeatedly - and Madinah is better for them. No one remains steadfast in it, patient over its hardship and severity until he dies, but I will be for him on the Day of Resurrection a witness or intercessor."
"3988","Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Subayh narrated to us, Abd Rabbihi ibn Rabiah narrated to me, from Abu al-Ward ibn Abi Burdah, from the servant of Abu Ayyub, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and stayed with Abu Ayyub; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lodged below, and Abu Ayyub above. When evening came and he spent the night, Abu Ayyub kept remembering that he was on the roof of a house with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) below him, between him and revelation. Abu Ayyub would not sleep, fearing dust would scatter upon him and his movement would harm him. In the morning he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had no sleep tonight, neither I nor Umm Ayyub. He said: Why, O Abu Ayyub? He said: I remembered that I am on the roof of a house with you below me; I move and dust scatters upon you and harms you, while I am between you and revelation. He said: Do not do so, O Abu Ayyub; shall I not teach you words, when you say them in the morning ten times and in the evening ten times, you are given ten good deeds for them, ten evil deeds are expiated for you, ten degrees are raised for you, and they will be for you on the Day of Resurrection like ten freed persons? You say: There is no god but Allah, to Him belongs dominion and praise, He has no partner."
"3989","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Sulayman, they said: Ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, Uthman ibn Jubayr, the freedman of Abu Ayyub, narrated to me, from Abu Ayyub, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me concisely. He said: When you stand in your prayer, pray the prayer of one bidding farewell, do not speak words you will apologize for, and gather despair of what is in people's hands."
"3990","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Bakr ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Uthman ibn Jubayr, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"3991","Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi and Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us, they said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us (h), and Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to me, they said: Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, Talhah ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The five prayers, Friday to Friday, and rendering trusts are expiation for what is between them. I said: What is rendering trusts? He said: Washing for impurity, for under every hair is impurity."
"3992","Ahmad ibn Mabahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hashim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hazmi, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them, played before him and in his lap. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you love them? He said: How should I not love them when they are my two basils of this world that I smell?"
"3993","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Qays, the storyteller of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Sirmah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Were it not that you sin, Allah would create a creation who sin and He forgives them."
"3994","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Umar, freedman of Ghufrah, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and He forgives them."
"3995","Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abbas, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Ayyub, that he opposed Marwan ibn al-Hakam in his prayer. Marwan said to him: What carries you to this? He said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray a prayer; if he agreed with him I agreed with you, and if he opposed him I prayed and returned to my family."
"3996","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me (h), and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Sufyan ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Asim ibn Sufyan, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution as commanded and prays as commanded is forgiven for what he did before. Is it so, O Uqbah ibn Amir? He said: Yes."
"3997","al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Abu Thabit Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Madini narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Alqamah ibn Sufyan ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi al-Taifi, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever performs ablution as commanded and prays as commanded is forgiven for his previous sins. Is it so, O Uqbah ibn Amir? He said: Yes."
"3998","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Asbagh narrated to us (h), and Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Sawadah, that Sufyan ibn Wahb narrated to him from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him food with greens containing onion or leek; he saw no trace of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) therein and refused to eat it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevented you from eating? He said: I saw no trace of you therein, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am shy before the angels of Allah, and it is not forbidden."
"3999","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashbah, from Yaqub ibn Afif ibn al-Musayyab, that he asked Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), about a man who prays in his house then comes to the mosque and reaches that prayer - does he repeat it with people or not? We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that? He said: Yes, he repeats it; that is for him a share of congregation."
"4000","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, that he heard Afif ibn Umar ibn al-Musayyab say: A man of Asad Khuzaymah narrated to me that he asked Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I pray the prayer in my house then come to the mosque, and prayer is established, so I pray with them, and I find something in myself from that. Abu Ayyub said: We asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: For that he has a share of congregation. Ahmad ibn Salih said: Ibn Wahb said Afif ibn Umar, and the correct is Afif ibn Amr; Malik narrated this hadith from Afif, saying Afif ibn Amr, and Malik did not raise it."
"4001","Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Bishr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah, who said: Abu Ayyub said to Marwan ibn al-Hakam: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not weep over religion when you entrust it to its people, but weep over it when you entrust it to other than its people."
"4002","Ahmad ibn Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr narrated to him that Abu Ishaq, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to him that they mentioned one day what is used for nabidh, and disputed about gourd. Abu Ayyub al-Ansari passed by them, so they sent a man to him. Abu Ayyub said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid every pitched vessel used for nabidh; he added nothing."
"4003","Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Tila, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that an animal be made a target."
"4004","Ahmad ibn Rishdin narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr narrated to him from his father, from Ubayd ibn Tila, who said: We raided with Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn al-Walid, and four sturdy non-Arabs of the enemy were brought, so he ordered them and they were killed patiently with arrows. That reached Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid killing by restraint."
"4005","Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Salih al-Marwazi narrated to us, Said ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from his father, from Ubayd ibn Tila, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid restraining a beast."
"4006","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Ubayd ibn Tila, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid restraining a beast."
"4007","Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Jafar narrated to me, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Tila, who said: I heard Abu Ayyub say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade restraining an animal; even if it were a chicken, I would not restrain it."
"4008","Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Imran ibn Abi Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Abu Ayyub, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on Friday: Whoever washes, touches perfume if he has it, wears of his best clothes, then goes out until he comes to the mosque, does not step over people's necks, and listens when the imam comes out and does not speak, he is forgiven for what is between it and the following Friday."
"4009","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Imran ibn Abi Yahya, from Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever washes on Friday, touches perfume if he has it, wears of his best clothes, then goes out until he comes to the mosque, prays what seems to him, harms no one, then listens when the imam comes out, it is expiation for what is between it and the next Friday."
"4010","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Imran ibn Abi Yahya al-Taymi, that Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik al-Sulami narrated to us that Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever washes on Friday and touches perfume, then mentioned the like of it."
"4011","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah in every state, and let the one who hears him say: May Allah have mercy on you, and he replies to him: May Allah guide you and set right your state."
"4012","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Shaybah narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."
"4013","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us (h), and Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Asadi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he had a pantry, and a ghoul would come and enter. He complained of it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you see it, say: In the name of Allah, answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It came, so he said that to it and seized it. It said: I will not return, so he released it, then it came to him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What did your captive do? He said: I seized it, and it said: I will not return, so I released it. He said: It will return. He seized it two or three times, each time it saying: I will not return, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come and say: What did your captive do? He would say: I seized it and it said: I will not return. He would say: It will return. He seized it, and it said: Release me and I will teach you something you say and nothing will come near you: Ayat al-Kursi. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: She spoke truth though she is a liar."
"4014","Ahmad ibn al-Jarud al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim Shadhan narrated to us, Sad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I had date-palms in a pantry of mine, and I saw it decreasing, so I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You will find therein tomorrow a cat, so say: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Next day I found therein a cat, and said: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It turned into an old woman and said: I remind you by Allah to leave me, for I will not return. I left her, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What did the man and his captive do? I informed him of her news. He said: She lied; she will return. Say to her: Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She turned into an old woman and said: I remind you by Allah, O Abu Ayyub, to leave me this time, for I will not return. I left her, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said to me as he had said. I said that three times. On the third she said to me: I remind you by Allah, O Abu Ayyub, to leave me until I teach you something no devil hears and enters that house. I said: What is it? She said: Ayat al-Kursi; no devil hears it but goes away. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She spoke truth though she is a liar."
"4015","Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I caught a female jinn, and she said to me: Leave me, and I will teach you something, when you say it none of us will harm you. He said: I said: What is it? She said: Ayat al-Kursi: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer. I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She spoke truth though she is a liar."
"4016","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Abu Farwah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I was harmed by an intruder of the house, so I complained of that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). There was a skylight in a house of ours, so he said: Watch for him; when you see something, say: Be gone, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you. He said: I watched, and something dangled from the skylight, so I leapt to it and said: Be gone, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you, and I seized him. He pleaded to me and said to me: I will not return. He said: I released him. In the morning I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What did your captive do? I informed him of what happened. He said: He will return. He said: I did that three times, each time seizing him and informing the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what happened. On the third I seized him, then said: You will not leave me until I bring you to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He adjured me and pleaded, saying: I will teach you something, when you say it at night no jinn or thief will come near you. He said: You recite Ayat al-Kursi. He said: I released him, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What did your captive do? I said: O Messenger of Allah, he adjured me and pleaded until I pitied him, and taught me something I say, when I say it no jinn or thief comes near me. He said: He spoke truth though he is a liar."
"4017","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says after the dawn prayer ten times: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things capable, they will be for him equal to four necks of the children of Ismail."
"4018","Abu Khalifah narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, all from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things capable, ten times, they will be for him equal to ten freed persons. The wording is of the hadith of Abd al-Wahhab."
"4019","Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things capable, it will be for him like one or two freed persons."
"4020","Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Asbahani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Shabi, who said: We were with al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, and he narrated that day that whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, He gives life and death, and He is over all things capable, once or ten times, that will equal for him a neck or ten necks. I said: From whom did you hear it? He said: From Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. I came to him and he narrated. I said: From whom did you hear it? He said: From Abu Ayyub narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4021","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"4022","Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things capable, they will be for him equal to ten necks of the children of Ismail, peace be upon him."
"4023","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, who said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, He gives life and death, and He is over all things capable, it is like one who freed four persons of the children of Ismail. He said: I said to al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym: From whom did you hear it? He said: From Amr ibn Maymun. I came to Amr ibn Maymun and said: From whom did you hear it? He said: From Ibn Abi Layla. I came to Ibn Abi Layla and said: From whom did you hear it? He said: From Abu Ayyub al-Ansari narrating it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4024","al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, who said: I heard al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, and mentioned with him: There is no man who says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things capable, but they will be for him equal to four necks. He said: I said to al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym: By Allah, I do not admire your saying about it; I see it better than four and four hundred. I said to al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym: Who informed you of this? He said: Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi informed me. I met Amr ibn Maymun and said to him: Did you inform al-Rabi of such and such? He said: Yes. I said: From whom did you hear that? He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla informed me. I met Abd al-Rahman and said: Amr ibn Maymun informed me of such and such. He said: He spoke truth; I informed him of it. I said: From whom do you narrate it? He said: From Abu Ayyub, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4025","Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumani narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn narrated to us, they said: Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, He has no partner, to Him belongs dominion and praise, and He is over all things capable, it is like freeing four persons of the children of Ismail."
"4026","Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Hafs al-Sadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Say, He is Allah, One, equals a third of the Quran."
"4027","Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tustari narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Anbasah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Say, He is Allah, One, is a third of the Quran."
"4028","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Rabi ibn Khuthaym, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a woman of the Ansar, who said: Abu Ayyub said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to recite in a night a third of the Quran? We feared he would command us with a matter we cannot do, so we fell silent. He said: Is one of you unable to recite in a night a third of the Quran? We feared he would command us with a matter we cannot do, so we fell silent. He said: Is one of you unable to recite in a night a third of the Quran? Whoever recites in a night: Allah, the One, the Eternal, has recited his night with a third of the Quran."
"4029","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, from a woman of the Ansar, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to recite in a night a third of the Quran? We fell silent. He said it three times and fell silent, then said: Whoever recites in a night: Say, He is Allah, One, has recited a third of the Quran."
"4030","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Amr ibn Maymun, from al-Rabi ibn Khuthaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a woman of the Ansar, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"4031","Muadh ibn al-Muthanna and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Musaddad narrated to us (h), and Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ammi narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a woman of the Ansar, that Abu Ayyub came to them and said: Do you not hear what good the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought? They said: How much good has the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought? He said: Who recites in a night a third of the Quran? We feared it and fell silent. He repeated it to us three times. He said: Whoever recites Say, He is One, it is as if it equals a third of the Quran."
"4032","Ali ibn Said al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah and al-Aswad, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will kill Ammar."
"4033","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salm al-Razi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from al-Qartha al-Dabbi, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray four rakahs before noon when the sun declines. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer? He said: The gates of heaven are opened at the decline of the sun until noon is prayed, and I love that a righteous deed be raised for me therein."
"4034","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ubaydah ibn Mutib al-Dabbi, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qazaah, from al-Qartha al-Dabbi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, about the four before noon, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this prayer you persist in when the sun declines? He said: O Abu Ayyub, the gates of heaven are opened at the decline of the sun, and the gates of heaven are not closed until noon is prayed. He said: Does he recite in them? He said: Yes. He said: Does he separate between them with salutation? He said: No."
"4035","Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qazaah, from al-Qartha, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to persist in four rakahs before noon when the sun declines, then mentioned the like of it."
"4036","Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qazaah, from al-Qartha al-Dabbi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to maintain four rakahs at the decline of the sun, then mentioned the like of it."
"4037","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, al-Masud narrated to us, from Abd al-Khaliq, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qartha or Ibn Qartha, from Abu Ayyub, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with me, I saw him maintain four before noon, and he said: When the sun declines, the gates of heaven are opened, and no gate of them is closed until noon is prayed, so I love that good be raised for me in that hour."
"4038","Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit al-Dahhan narrated to us, al-Mufaddal al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Said ibn Masruq, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from al-Qartha, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are these four rakahs? He said: This is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened and not closed until noon is prayed, so I love to send forth."
"4039","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Ali ibn al-Salt, from Abu Ayyub, that he used to pray four before noon. It was said to him? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray them, so I asked him. He said: It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, so I love that a righteous deed rise for me therein."
"4040","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Ali ibn al-Salt, from Abu Ayyub, that he used to pray four before noon. It was said to him: What is this prayer? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray them, so I asked him. He said: It is an hour in which the gates of heaven are opened, so I love that a righteous deed be raised for me therein."
"4041","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Ali ibn al-Salt, who said: I saw Abu Ayyub remove his two leather socks and they looked at him. He said: I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over them, but ablution is beloved to me."
"4042","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah and Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Ali ibn Mudrik, who said: I saw Abu Ayyub remove his two leather socks and they looked at him. He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wipe over them, but ablution is beloved to me."
"4043","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shabib al-Assal al-Asbahani narrated to us, Ismail ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, who said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari raided the land of Rome, and when he became heavy he said: When I die, carry me with you; when you face the enemy, bury me under your feet. I will narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); were I not in this state I would not narrate it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies testifying that there is no god but Allah enters Paradise."
"4044","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from some of their elders who said: We were with Abu Ayyub in the land of Rome, and he fell ill and enjoined us: Carry me until, when you face the enemy, bury me under your feet. Then he said: I will narrate to you a hadith; were I not in this state I would not narrate it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise."
"4045","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil al-Sarraj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, who said: Yala ibn Ubayd informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"4046","Abu Husayn al-Qadi narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from their elders, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"4047","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from their elders, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise."
"4048","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abayah ibn Ribi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her: Do you not know that Allah looked upon the people of the earth and chose your father from them and sent him as a prophet, then looked a second time and chose your husband, so He revealed to me and I married him to you and took him as successor?"
"4049","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abayah, from Abu Ayyub that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, and Fatimah, may Allah be pleased with her, came to visit him while he was recovering from his illness. When she saw the hardship upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the hadith at length."
"4050","Ahmad ibn Mabahram al-Idhaji narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar narrated to us, Nail ibn Najih narrated to us, Fitr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and a feather fell upon his beard, so Abu Ayyub hastened to him and took it from his beard. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: May Allah remove from you what you dislike."
"4051","al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Hasirah, from Abu Sadiq, from Mihnaf ibn Sulaym, who said: We came to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari while he fed horses of his at Sanba, and we stayed midday with him. I said to him: O Abu Ayyub, you fought the polytheists with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then you come to fight the Muslims? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to fight three: the breakers, the unjust, and the renegades. I have fought the breakers and the unjust, and I will fight, God willing, the renegades at the mountain paths, roads, and Nahrawans, and I do not know who they are?"
"4052","Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqaqi narrated to us, Abu Rabiah Fahd ibn Awf narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr Jafar ibn Iyas, from al-Hajjaj ibn Muhajir, from Zubayd or Ruyayd, from Abu Ayyub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An angel is in a station from me in which none of you is, and I dislike that he find from me the smell of anything."
"4053","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Zuhri, from Hakim ibn Bashir, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is charity upon a hostile relative."
"4054","Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Hanash ibn al-Harith, from Riyah ibn al-Harith, who said: While Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, sat in al-Rahbah, a man came with traces of travel upon him and said: Peace upon you, O my master. It was said: Who is this? He said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. He said: Abu Ayyub, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever I am his master, Ali is his master."
"4055","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us, Ali ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hanash ibn al-Harith and from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Riyah ibn al-Harith (h), and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam, from Riyah ibn al-Harith al-Nakhai, who said: We sat with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, and a group of Ansar came wearing turbans, saying: Peace upon you, O our master. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I am your master and you are Arab people? They said: Yes, we heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever I am his master, Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. This is Abu Ayyub among us. Abu Ayyub uncovered the turban from his face. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomever I am his master, Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him."
"4056","Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Surah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Abi Nuaym, from Abdullah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beef broth containing garlic, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found the smell of garlic and said: Take it out. He said: Why, O Messenger of Allah, is it forbidden? He said: No, but Gabriel converses with me."
"4057","Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us, Amr ibn Hashim al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah, from Abu Shuayb al-Hadrami, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you defecates, let him wipe with three stones, for that suffices him."
"4058","Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, who narrated to him that he heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while we were in Madinah: I have been informed of the caravan of Abu Sufyan approaching; will you go out before this caravan? Perhaps Allah will grant it to us as spoils. We said: Yes. He went out and we went out. When we marched a day or two, he said to us: What do you think about the people, for they have been informed of your going out? We said: By Allah, we have no strength to fight the enemy, but we intended the caravan. Then he said: What do you think about fighting the people? We said the like of that. Al-Miqdad ibn Amr said: Then we will not say to you, O Messenger of Allah, as the people of Musa said to Musa: Go, you and your Lord, and fight; we sit here. He said: We, the Ansar, wished we had said as al-Miqdad said, dearer to us than great wealth. Allah revealed upon His Messenger: As your Lord brought you out of your house in truth, while a party of the believers disliked. They dispute with you about the truth after it became clear, as if driven to death while they look. Then Allah revealed: I am with you, so make firm those who believe; I will cast terror into the hearts of those who disbelieve, so strike above the necks and strike every fingertip. And He said: When Allah promises you one of the two parties, that it is yours, and you wish that the unarmed one be yours. Thorn means the people, and unarmed means the caravan. When He promised us one of the two parties, either the people or the caravan, our souls were pleased. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to see what was before the people? He said: I saw darkness and do not know. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are they; come, let us count. We did, and we were three hundred and thirteen men. We informed the Messenger of Allah of our number, and that pleased him, so he praised Allah and said: The number of the companions of Talut. Then we met the people and lined up; an impulse darted from us before the line, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at them and said: With me, with me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I adjure You Your promise. Ibn Rawahah said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to advise you, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is better to advise than him; Allah is greater than that You adjure Him His promise. He said: O Ibn Rawahah, I will adjure Allah His promise, for Allah does not break the appointment. He took a handful of dust and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw it in the faces of the people, and they were defeated. Allah revealed: You did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw. We killed and captured. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not see that you should have captives, for we are only callers conciliating. We, the Ansar, said: Only envy for us carries Umar to what he said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept, then woke, then said: Call Umar for me. He was called, and he said: Allah has revealed upon me: It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has thoroughly subdued in the land; you desire the goods of this world, while Allah desires the Hereafter, and Allah is Mighty, Wise."
"4059","Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, from Abu Ayyub, who said: We used to pray Maghrib when the sun set."
"4060","Abu Habib Yahya ibn Nafi al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, who said: Abu Ayyub said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Pray the Maghrib prayer with the setting of the sun; hasten it before the rising of the star."
"4061","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, from Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, from Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Taymi, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, that he heard Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"4062","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri, from Haywah ibn Shurayh and Ibn Lahiah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Aslam Abu Imran, from Abu Ayyub, who said: We said among ourselves, some of us to others, secretly from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Our wealth has been neglected, so if only we would stay back with it. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed in His Book, refuting what we had intended: And spend in the way of Allah and do not cast yourselves with your own hands into destruction — concerning staying back with wealth and tending it while abandoning jihad and spending in the way of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"4063","Abu Sawrah, the nephew of Abu Ayyub, from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman, (ha) and narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, both from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: How excellent are the mutakhallilun. They said: Who are the mutakhallilun, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Those who pick with the khilal in ablution, and those who pick with the khilal after food. As for the khilal of ablution: rinsing the mouth, sniffing water into the nose, and between the fingers; and as for the khilal of food: clearing it from the food, for there is nothing harder upon the two angels than to see something between the teeth of their companion while he stands praying."
"4064","Narrated Muhammad ibn Yahya Mandah al-Asbahani, from Abdah ibn Abd Allah, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Rabah ibn Amr al-Qaysi, from Abu Yahya al-Raqashi, from Abu Sawrah, the nephew of Abu Ayyub, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: How excellent are the mutakhallilun in food and ablution."
"4065","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Ahmad ibn Janab al-Missisi, from Isa ibn Yunus, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a nephew who does not refrain from the unlawful. He said: What of his religion? He said: He prays and declares Allah one. He said: Ask him to grant you his religion as a gift; if he refuses, buy it from him. The man sought that from him but he refused him. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: I found him miserly with his religion. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: Indeed Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills."
"4066","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Said ibn Anbasah, from al-Qasim ibn Malik, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Announcing oneself is that you call the servant until the people of the house you seek permission from take notice."
"4067","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the salam — what is the announcing? He said: He said: A man utters a tasbih, a takbir and a tahmid, and clears his throat, notifying the people of the house."
"4068","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to use the siwak at night two or three times."
"4069","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood at night, prayed four rakahs without speaking or commanding anything, giving the salam between every two rakahs."
"4070","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi, from my father, from Wasil ibn al-Saib al-Raqashi, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he sniffed water into his nose three times, rinsed his mouth, put his two fingers into his mouth, reached with his palms when washing his face to the front of his ears, wiped with his fingers the back of his ears along with his head when wiping his head, and ran his fingers through his beard."
"4071","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil, from al-Hasan ibn Hammad, from Jabir ibn Nuh, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The people of Paradise visit one another upon white riding camels as though they are rubies; and there is nothing in Paradise of beasts except camels and birds."
"4072","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah and from Abu Sawrah, from his uncle Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who are these about whom Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: Men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves? He said: They used water for istinja and they did not sleep the whole night."
"4073","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib al-Taraifi, from Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan, from Said ibn Maslamah, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died, the polytheists walked to one another and said: This renegade has been cut off tonight. So Allah, the Exalted, revealed: Indeed We have granted you al-Kawthar, to the end of the surah."
"4074","And from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about tasir, and he said: A twisting in the side of the mouth."
"4075","And from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about al-shaf and al-watr, and he said: Two days and a night: the day of Arafah, the day of sacrifice, and al-watr is the night of sacrifice, the night of Jam."
"4076","And from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: Mudhammatan, and he said: Two dark green ones."
"4077","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Muawiyah, from my father, from Wasil ibn al-Saib, from Abu Sawrah, from Abu Ayyub, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I love horses — are there horses in Paradise? He said: When you enter Paradise, you will be brought a horse of ruby with two wings; you will be carried upon it and it will fly with you in Paradise wherever you wish."
"4078","Ziyad ibn Anum from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Bishr ibn Musa, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum, who said: I heard my father Ziyad ibn Anum say: An anchorage of theirs at sea brought them together with the ship of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. He said: Whenever our meal came, we sent to Abu Ayyub and the people of his ship. Abu Ayyub came and said: You invited me while I am fasting, and it was my duty to answer you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Muslim owes his Muslim brother six obligatory traits; whoever abandons one of them has abandoned an obligatory right of his brother: when he invites him, to answer him; when he meets him, to greet him with peace; when he sneezes, to invoke mercy for him; when he falls ill, to visit him; when he dies, to follow his funeral; and when he seeks his counsel, to counsel him. My father said: Among us was a jesting man, and a man was in charge of our provisions. The jester would say to the one in charge of the food: May Allah reward you with good and piety. When he did it excessively, he became angry and insulted him. The jester said: O Abu Ayyub, what do you think of a man — when I say to him: May Allah reward you with good and piety — he gets angry and insults me? Abu Ayyub said: We used to say: Whoever is not reformed by good is reformed by evil, so turn it around on him. When the man came, the jester said to him: May Allah reward you with evil and hardship. The man laughed and was pleased, and said: You never leave your idleness in any case. The jester said: May Allah reward Abu Ayyub with good and piety, for he told me so."
"4079","Sufyan ibn Wahb from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, from Asbagh ibn al-Faraj, (ha) and narrated Ahmad ibn Rushdin, from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, that Sufyan ibn Wahb told him, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that food was sent to Abu Ayyub with greens containing onions or leeks; he saw no trace of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it, so he refused to eat it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What prevented you from eating? He said: I did not see your trace in it, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am shy before the angels of Allah, but it is not unlawful."
"4080","Abd Allah ibn Yazid Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik al-Maafiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An evening going or a morning going in the way of Allah is better than all upon which the sun has risen and set."
"4081","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Shurahbil ibn Sharik al-Maafiri, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, who said: I heard Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going in the way of Allah or an evening going is better than all upon which the sun has risen and set."
"4082","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam, from Ibn Wahb, from Huyayy ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever separates a mother from her child, Allah will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection."
"4083","Narrated Abu al-Jarud Masud ibn Muhammad al-Ramli, from Imran ibn Harun al-Sufi, from Ibn Lahiah, from Zuhrah ibn Mabad, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he supplicated, would begin with himself."
"4084","Narrated Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih, from Asbagh ibn al-Faraj, from Abd Allah ibn Wahb, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abu Aqil Zuhrah ibn Mabad, (ha) and narrated Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi, from Muhriz ibn Awn, from Rishdin ibn Sad, from Zuhrah ibn Mabad, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate or drank, he would say: Praise be to Allah who fed, gave drink, made it go down with ease, and made for it a way out."
"4085","Abu al-Khayr Marthad ibn Abd Allah al-Yazani from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from my father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Marthad ibn Abd Allah al-Yazani, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: My community will remain upon good — or upon the fitrah — so long as they do not delay the Maghrib until the stars intermingle."
"4086","Abu Tamim al-Jayshani from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, from Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This prayer — meaning al-Asr — was enjoined upon those before you and they neglected it; whoever among you guards it today is given its reward twice over, and there is no prayer after it until the witness appears — meaning the star."
"4087","Abu al-Shimal ibn Dibab from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, from Ali ibn al-Madini, (ha) and narrated Abu Khalifah, from Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar, both saying: narrated Hafs ibn Ghiyath, (ha) and narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi, from Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Awaqi, (ha) and narrated Ahmad ibn al-Qasim al-Jawhari, from Said ibn Sulayman, both saying: narrated Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Makhul, from Abu al-Shimal ibn Dibab, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are of the sunnahs of the messengers: modesty, perfuming, marriage, and the siwak."
"4088","Sulayman ibn Farrukh from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Yusuf al-Qadi and al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz al-Basri, both saying: narrated Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, from Quraysh ibn Hayyan al-Ijli, from Sulayman ibn Farrukh, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the tidings of heaven. He said: You ask me about the tidings of heaven while you leave your nails like the claws of birds, with filth and dirt gathering in them."
"4089","Abd al-Rahman al-Hazmi from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Ubayd ibn Kathir al-Tammar al-Kufi, from Dirar ibn Surad, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Hazmi, from his father, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are to me in the station of Harun to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me."
"4090","Abu Muhammad al-Hadrami from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, from Musaddad, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ward, from Abu Muhammad al-Hadrami, from Abu Ayyub, who said: A man said in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Praise be to Allah, much, good and blessed therein. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the utterer of the words? The man fell silent, thinking that something he disliked had befallen him from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is he? For he said nothing but right. The man said: It is I who said it, O Messenger of Allah, hoping for good thereby. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I saw thirteen angels racing with your words, which of them would raise them to Allah, the Blessed and Exalted."
"4091","Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, from Musaddad, from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ward, from Abu Muhammad al-Hadrami, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Shall I not teach you, O Abu Ayyub? I said: Yes indeed. He said: Say in the morning: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, without partner — ten times. No Muslim servant says them ten times but Allah writes for him thereby ten good deeds, erases from him thereby ten evil deeds, and they are better with Allah on the Day of Resurrection than freeing ten slaves; and he does not say them in the evening but Allah writes for him the like of that."
"4092","Narrated al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi, from Ishaq ibn Abi Israil, from Abd al-Ala, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ward, from Abu Muhammad al-Hadrami, from Abu Ayyub, who said: I prepared for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr food enough for them both, and I brought it to them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go and invite for me thirty of the nobles of the Ansar. That weighed heavily upon me; I said: I have nothing to add to it, as though I feigned inattention. He said: Go and invite for me thirty of the nobles of the Ansar. So I invited them and they came. He said: Eat. They ate until they were satisfied, then testified that he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. Then he said: Go and invite for me sixty of the nobles of the Ansar. Abu Ayyub said: By Allah, I am more generous with sixty than with thirty. He said: So I invited them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hold back. They ate until they were satisfied, then testified that he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. Then he said: Go and invite for me ninety of the Ansar. He said: I am indeed more generous with the ninety and the sixty than with the thirty. He said: So I invited them; they ate until they were satisfied, then testified that he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then pledged allegiance to him before leaving. One hundred and eighty men ate of that food of mine, all of them of the Ansar."
"4093","Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi, from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from Baqiyyah, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Ansar cast lots for their dwellings as to which of them would shelter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu Ayyub won them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with him. Whenever food was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would take some of it, then send it to us."
"4094","Abd Allah ibn Yaish from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Abu Khalifah, from Ali ibn al-Madini, from Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad, from my father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, from Abd Allah ibn Yaish, from Abu Ayyub, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ten — whoever says them after his prayers when he has prayed: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things — Allah writes for him thereby ten good deeds, erases from him thereby ten evil deeds, raises him thereby ten degrees, they equal ten necks freed, and they are a guard for him against Satan until evening; and whoever says them in the evening, it is the like of that until morning."
"4095","Al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, from Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that he said while in the land of Byzantium: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He has power over all things — ten times — Allah writes for him ten good deeds, erases from him ten evil deeds, they equal ten necks, and Allah shields him from Satan; and whoever says them in the evening, it is the like of that."
"4096","Mahfuz ibn Alqamah from Abu Ayyub. Narrated Musa ibn Jumhur al-Tinnisi, from Muhammad ibn Musaffa, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from Nasr ibn Alqamah, from his brother Mahfuz ibn Alqamah, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever meets the enemy and is patient until he is killed or overcomes is not put to trial in his grave."
"4097","Khalid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Salamah al-Khuzai. Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, from Abu Malik ibn Abi Farah al-Khuzai, who said: My father told me, from his father, from his grandfather Masud ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Salamah, mentioning that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted upon him at al-Jiranah, slaughtered a camel for him, shaded with him and Khalid spent the evening with him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for the umrah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Muharrish descended to the valley until they reached a place called Ashqab. He said: O Muharrish, the water of this place up to al-Kurr is for Khalid, and what remains of the valley is yours, O Muharrish. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug into al-Kurr with his hand and water gushed from it and he drank. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for the umrah and sent Khalid to one of his companions called Muharrish ibn Abd Allah — the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that day fearing entry into Makkah — and he took him by a road turning him away from what he feared of that, which he knew, until he completed his rites; and they returned to Khalid in the morning, and Muharrish released him from ihram — meaning shaved him."
"4098","Khalid ibn Zayd al-Ansari. Narrated Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Madini al-Misri, from Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi, from Umar ibn Yahya al-Muqaddami, from Mujammi ibn Yahya ibn Harithah, who said: I heard my uncle Khalid ibn Zayd al-Ansari say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is free of miserliness who pays zakat, entertains the guest, and gives in calamity."
"4099","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal al-Makki, from Yaqub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, from Fadlalah ibn Yaqub, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi, from Mujammi ibn Yahya, from his uncle Khalid ibn Zayd ibn Jariyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three — whoever has them in him is shielded from the miserliness of his soul: whoever pays zakat, entertains the guest, and gives in calamity."
"4100","Khalid ibn Urfutah al-Udhri, and Udhrah is of Qudaah; he was the deputy of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas over Kufah, then Ziyad employed him over Kufah. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus, from Abd Allah ibn Idris, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Khalifah ibn Qays, from Khalid — and Sad had left him as deputy over Kufah."
"4101","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Affan ibn Muslim, (ha) and narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, both saying: narrated Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, (ha) and narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, from Asad ibn Musa, all saying: narrated Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Khalid ibn Urfutah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Khalid, there will be tribulation, events, disagreement and division; when that comes, if you can be the one killed and not the killer, do so."
"4102","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail and Shihab ibn Abbad, (ha) and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, all saying: narrated Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from Muslim the freedman of Khalid ibn Urfutah, from Khalid ibn Urfutah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"4103","Narrated Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi, from Abu Umar Hafs ibn Umar al-Hawdi, from Shubah, (ha) and narrated Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi, from Umar ibn Marzuq, from Shubah, from Jami ibn Shaddad, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Yasar say: I was sitting with Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah when it reached them that a man had died of a stomach ailment; one of them said to the other: Has it not reached you — or did you not hear — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be tormented in his grave. He said: Yes indeed."
"4104","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, from Said ibn Sulayman, from Ayyub ibn Jabir, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar al-Juhani, who said: Sulayman ibn Surad said to Khalid ibn Urfutah: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be tormented in his grave? Khalid said: Yes."
"4105","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi, (ha) and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Abu Husayn al-Qadi, both saying: narrated Yahya al-Himmani, both saying: narrated Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, who said: A man of Juhaynah died on a hot day; in the morning I sat with Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah and they said: What prevented you from informing us of the funeral of the righteous man so we could attend it? We said: It was hot and the man suffered from his belly. One of them said to his companion: Did you not hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be tormented in his grave? He said: Yes indeed."
"4106","Narrated al-Miqdam ibn Dawud, from Ali ibn Mabad, from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu Sakhrah, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, who said: I was sitting with Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah when it reached them that a man had died of his belly; one of them said to the other: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be tormented in his grave? He said: Yes indeed."
"4107","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti, from Abu Shaybah, from Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, that he heard Sulayman ibn Surad saying to Khalid ibn Urfutah: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be tormented in his grave? He said: Yes."
"4108","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, from al-Hasan ibn Yunus al-Zayyat, from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Yazid ibn Abi Khalid, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar, who said: I was sitting with Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah when one of them said to his companion: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be tormented in his grave?"
"4109","Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi, from Muhammad ibn Nubatah al-Razi, (ha) and narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi, from Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Yazid al-Khazzaz al-Razi, both saying: narrated Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqri, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ibn Ashwa, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar al-Juhani, who said: A man of ours who suffered from his belly died, and we buried him early. I came to the mosque and found Sulayman ibn Surad and Khalid ibn Urfutah. Sulayman said: What prevented you from informing us of your companion? I said: He suffered from his belly so we buried him early. Sulayman ibn Surad said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sufferer of the belly is not tormented in the grave — do you testify, O Khalid? He said: Yes indeed."
"4110","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi, from Salamah ibn al-Fadl, from Anbasah ibn Said, from Said ibn Ashwa, from Abd Allah ibn Yasar al-Juhani, who said: We had a dead man and we hastened with him. I came to the mosque and Khalid ibn Urfutah and Sulayman ibn Surad met me and said: Did you not inform us of him? I said: He suffered from his belly. They said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The sufferer of the belly is not tormented in his grave."
"4111","Narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji, from Ubayd ibn Asbat, from my father, (ha) and narrated Asbat ibn Muhammad, from my father, from my grandfather, from Abu Sinan al-Shaybani, from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii, who said: Khalid ibn Urfutah said to Sulayman ibn Surad — or Sulayman ibn Surad said to Khalid ibn Urfutah: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed by his belly will not be tormented in his grave? One of them said to his companion: Yes."
"4112","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri and Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti, all saying: narrated Abu Kurayb, (ha) and narrated Zakariya ibn Yahya al-Saji, from Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Ziyadi, both saying: narrated al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Karim al-Urfuti, from Abu Khalid al-Bazzaz, from Kilab ibn Amr, from his father, from Khalid ibn Urfutah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah raising his hands, saying: O Allah, bless the horses of Ahmas and their men."
"4113","Narrated al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi al-Asbahani, from Abbad ibn Yaqub al-Asadi, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Shaqiq ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Umarah ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Urfutah, who said: We were with Khalid ibn Urfutah on the day al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, was killed, and Khalid said to us: This is what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: You will be tried concerning my household after me."
"4114","Khalid Abu Nafi al-Khuzai. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abu Kurayb, from Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Said ibn Tariq, from Nafi ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from his father — and he was of the people of the Tree, (ha) and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, from Ali ibn al-Madini, from Marwan ibn Muawiyah, (ha) and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, from Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam — all from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Nafi ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from his father — and he was of the people of the Tree — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer one day, lightened it, and sat, prolonging the sitting. When he finished, we said: O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the sitting in your prayer. He said: It is a prayer of hope and fear; I asked Allah in it for three traits: He granted me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to destroy you with a torment that befell those before you, and He granted it to me; I asked Him not to set over your community an enemy to overrun it, and He granted it to me; and I asked Him not to clothe you in factions and make some of you taste the might of others, and He withheld it from me."
"4115","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abu Kurayb, from Yahya ibn Zakariya ibn Abi Zaidah, from Sad ibn Tariq, from Nafi ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from his father, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with people looking on, he prayed a light prayer complete in bowing and prostration."
"4116","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abu Kurayb, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Abu Malik al-Ashjai, from Nafi ibn Khalid al-Khuzai, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with people around him, he prayed a light prayer complete in bowing and prostration. One day he sat and prolonged the sitting until some of us gestured to one another to be silent, for revelation was coming to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he finished, some of the people said: O Messenger of Allah, you prolonged the sitting until some of us gestured to one another that revelation was descending upon you. He said: No, but it is a prayer of hope and fear; I asked Allah in it for three things: He granted me two and withheld one from me. I asked Him not to torment you with a torment He inflicted upon those before you, and I asked Him not to set over your generality an enemy to violate it, and He granted them to me; and I asked Him not to clothe you in factions and make some of you taste the might of others, and He withheld it from me. I said to him: Did your father hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I heard him say: He heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — the number of these ten fingers of mine."
"4117","Khalid ibn Said ibn al-As, may Allah be pleased with him. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri: that Abu Bakr after the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched commanders to Sham and put Khalid ibn Said in command of a troop."
"4118","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Yahya al-Himmani, from Khalid ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As, who said: I heard my father mention, from Khalid ibn Said, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen and said: Whomever you pass of the Arabs and hear the adhan among them, do not molest him; and whomever you do not hear the adhan among, call them to Islam — if they do not answer, fight them."
"4119","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, both saying: narrated Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban, (ha) and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Yahya al-Himmani, from Khalid ibn Said ibn al-As, who said: I heard my father mention, from his uncle Khalid ibn Said, who said: He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he arrived from the emigration to Abyssinia, with his daughter Umm Khalid. He brought her to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a yellow shirt that pleased the girl; she had understood some of the speech of Abyssinia, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to her in the Abyssinian tongue: Sanah sanah — which in Abyssinian means: good. Then he said to her: Wear out and replace, then wear out and replace. He said: By Allah, she wore out then replaced, then wore out then replaced. Then she leaned toward the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed her hand upon the place of the seal of prophethood; her father moved her away, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave her."
"4120","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, both saying: narrated Yahya al-Himmani, from Ishaq ibn Said ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-As, from his father Said ibn Amr, from Khalid ibn Said, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a ring on his hand. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Khalid, what is this ring? He said: A ring I have taken. He said: Throw it to me. He said: So I threw it to him, and it was an iron ring colored with silver. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is its inscription? I said: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and wore it, and it is the ring that was in his hand."
"4121","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Suwayd ibn Said, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Umawi, from his grandfather Said, from Khalid ibn Said, who said: My father fell gravely ill and said: If Allah heals me of this ailment of mine, the god of Muhammad ibn Abi Kabshah shall not be worshipped in the belly of Makkah. Khalid said: So he perished."
"4122","Khalid ibn al-As ibn Hashim ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Shayban ibn Farrukh, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the plague befalls a land and you are in it, do not leave fleeing from it; and when it befalls a land and you are not in it, do not enter it."
"4123","Khalid ibn Hakim ibn Hizam. Narrated Bishr ibn Musa, from al-Humaydi, (ha) and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, both saying: narrated Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Najih, from Khalid ibn Hakim ibn Hizam, that Abu Ubaydah, may Allah be pleased with him, seized a man of the people of the land, and Khalid ibn Hakim, may Allah be pleased with him, forbade him from him. They said to Khalid: You have angered Abu Ubaydah. He said: I did not anger him, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The most severely tormented of people toward people in this world are the most severely tormented with Allah on the Day of Resurrection."
"4124","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abu Kurayb, from Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Najih, that Khalid ibn Hakim passed by Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah while he was tormenting people over the jizyah, and said to him: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The most severely tormented of people on the Day of Resurrection are the most severe of them in torment in this world. He said: Go and let them go."
"4125","Khalid ibn al-Hawari al-Habashi. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjuman, from Ishaq ibn al-Harith, who said: I saw Khalid ibn al-Hawari, a man of Abyssinia of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), visit his family; when he finished, death came upon him and he said: Wash me two washings: a washing for janabah and a washing for death."
"4126","Khalid ibn Adi al-Juhani. Narrated Bishr ibn Musa, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, from Said ibn Ayyub, from Abu al-Aswad, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Busr ibn Said, from Khalid ibn Adi al-Juhani, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever receives a kindness from his brother without asking or aspiring, let him accept it and not refuse it, for it is only provision Allah has driven to him."
"4127","Khalid ibn Abi Khalid, unattributed. Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Dirar ibn Surad, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father: concerning the naming of those of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who stood with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Khalid ibn Abi Khalid."
"4128","Khalid ibn Abi Jabal al-Adwani. Narrated Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi, from my father, (ha) and narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Yahya ibn Main, (ha) and narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar, from Hisham ibn Ammar, all saying: narrated Marwan ibn Muawiyah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Abi Jabal, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing upon a bow or a staff in the east of Thaqif, reciting By the heaven and the night-comer until he completed it; I memorized it in the Jahiliyyah while a polytheist, then I recited it in Islam."
"4129","And narrated Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari, from Zakariya ibn Adi, (ha) and narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl al-Razi, from Sahl ibn Uthman, all saying: narrated Marwan ibn Muawiyah, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid al-Adwani, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the east of Thaqif standing upon a bow or a staff when he came to them seeking support. He said: I heard him recite By the heaven and the night-comer until he completed it. He said: I memorized it in the Jahiliyyah while a polytheist, then I recited it in Islam. They said: What did you hear from this man? So I recited it to them, and those of Quraysh with them said: We know our companion best; had we known what he says is true, we would have followed him."
"4130","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari, from Abu Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid ibn Abi Jabal, from his father: that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came to them — meaning Thaqif — seeking support among them — and he mentioned the like of the hadith of Marwan."
"4131","Khalid ibn Ubayd al-Sulami. Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, from my father, (ha) and narrated Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariya al-Araj al-Iyadi, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Aqil ibn Mudrik, from al-Harith ibn Ubayd al-Sulami, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has granted you at your deaths a third of your wealth as an increase in your deeds."
"4132","Khalid ibn Abd Allah ibn Harmalah al-Mudliji, concerning whose companionship there is disagreement. Narrated Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki, from al-Qanabi, from Sahbal ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya, (ha) and narrated al-Husayn al-Tustari, from Amr ibn Hisham Abu Umayyah al-Harrani, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Sahbal ibn Muhammad al-Madani, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah ibn Harmalah al-Mudliji, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) halted at Usfan, and a man said: Would you like the noblest of women and the choicest of camels of Banu Mudlij? And among the people was a man of Banu Mudlij, and that showed upon his face. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of a people is the defender of his people so long as he does not sin."
"4133","Khalid ibn Abi Dujanah al-Ansari. Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Dirar ibn Surad, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father: concerning the naming of those of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who stood with Ali: Khalid ibn Abi Dujanah, may Allah be pleased with them."
"4134","Khuwaylid ibn Amr al-Ansari. Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Dirar ibn Surad, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father: concerning the naming of those of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who stood with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Khuwaylid ibn Amr al-Ansari, a Badri of Banu Salamah."
"4135","Khallad ibn al-Saib al-Ansari. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abu Kurayb, from Mahbub ibn Muhriz, (ha) and narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Imran al-Thalabi, from Jafar ibn Awn, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Khallad ibn al-Saib al-Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing of the crop or fruit of one of you is taken by bird or beast but he has reward therein."
"4136","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Salm ibn Junadah, from Waki, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Khallad ibn al-Saib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sows a crop and bird or beast eats from it, it is charity for him."
"4137","Khallad ibn Rafi al-Ansari. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti, from Yaqub ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran, from Rifaa ibn Yahya al-Ansari, from Muadh ibn Rifaa ibn Rafi, from his father, who said: My brother Khallad and I went out to Badr upon a lean camel of ours."
"4138","Kharijah ibn Hudhafah al-Adawi — he is Kharijah ibn Hudhafah ibn Ghanim ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf ibn Ubayd ibn Uwayj ibn Adi ibn Kab; he was among those who attended the conquest of Egypt and died there. Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam, from al-Layth ibn Sad, (ha) and narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, (ha) and narrated Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi, from Asim ibn Ali, (ha) and narrated Abu Khalifah, from Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, both saying: narrated Layth ibn Sad, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn Rashid al-Zawfi, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Murrah al-Zawfi, from Kharijah ibn Hudhafah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has reinforced you with a prayer better for you than red camels, made for you between the Isha prayer and the rising of dawn."
"4139","Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar, from Yazid ibn Harun, (ha) and narrated Musa ibn Isa ibn al-Mundhir al-Himsi, from Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi, both saying: narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd Allah ibn Rashid al-Zawfi, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Murrah al-Zawfi, from Kharijah ibn Hudhafah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us at the dawn prayer and said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has reinforced you tonight with a prayer better for you than red camels: al-Witr between the Isha prayer and the rising of dawn."
"4140","Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Abi Zuhayr, brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj. Narrated Musa ibn Zakariya al-Tustari, from Shabab al-Usfuri, from Bakr ibn Sulayman, who said: Abu Bakr alighted upon Habib ibn Isaf, brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj, at al-Sunh — and it is said: rather he alighted upon Kharijah ibn Zayd Abu Zuhayr, brother of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj."
"4141","Kharijah ibn Zayd al-Ansari. Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, from Hisham ibn Ammar, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Umayr ibn Hani, that al-Numan ibn Bashir told him, who said: A man of ours called Kharijah ibn Zayd died; we covered him with a cloth, and I stood to pray when I heard a clamor and turned, and there he was moving. He said: The boldest of the people, their middle one, Abd Allah; Umar, Commander of the Believers, strong in body, strong in the command of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic; Uthman ibn Affan, Commander of the Believers, chaste and modest, who pardons many sins. Two nights have passed and four remain; people differ and have no order. O people, turn to your imam, listen to him and obey. This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Ibn Rawahah. Then he said: What did Zayd ibn Kharijah do — meaning his father. Then he said: I took threads of injustice unjustly. Then the voice faded."
"4142","Kharijah ibn Amr al-Jumahi. Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Jarud al-Asbahani, from Abd Allah ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, from Abd Allah ibn Nafi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah al-Jumahi, from his father, from Kharijah ibn Amr al-Jumahi, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the Conquest while I was at his she-camel: There is no bequest for an heir; Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has given every holder of a right his right, and for the adulterer is the stone. Whoever claims for other than his father or takes as patrons other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people; Allah accepts from him neither sarf nor adl on the Day of Resurrection."
"4143","Khawwat ibn Jubayr al-Ansari, a Badri, kunya Abu Abd Allah — and it is said Abu Salih. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Khawwat ibn Jubayr is kunya'd Abu Salih."
"4144","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Dirar ibn Surad, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father: concerning the naming of those who stood with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Khawwat ibn Jubayr, a Badri of Banu Harithah who turned back on the way, for whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a share."
"4145","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Hisham al-Sadusi, from Ziyad ibn Abd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Khawwat ibn Jubayr ibn al-Numan ibn Umayyah ibn al-Bark — and al-Bark is Imru al-Qays ibn Thalabah ibn Amr ibn Awf — for whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck with his arrow and his reward on the day of Badr."
"4146","Narrated Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj, from Yahya ibn Bukayr, who said: Khawwat ibn Jubayr died in the year forty, at the age of seventy-four."
"4147","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr say: Khawwat ibn Jubayr died in the year forty."
"4148","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi, from Dawud ibn Mansur al-Qadi, from Jarir ibn Hazim, (ha) and narrated Abu Ghassan Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi, from al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad, from Wahb ibn Jarir, from my father, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Aslam narrate that Khawwat ibn Jubayr said: We alighted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Marr al-Zahran. He said: I came out of my tent and saw women talking; they pleased me, so I went back, took out my luggage, took out a suit from it, wore it, came and sat with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of his dome and said: Abu Abd Allah, what seats you with them? When I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I was awed and confounded. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a camel of mine has strayed and I seek a shackle for it. He went on and I followed him; he cast his cloak to me and entered the arak trees, as though I see the whiteness of his back amid the greenery of the arak. He relieved himself and performed ablution, then came with water flowing from his beard upon his chest — or he said: dripping from his beard upon his chest — and said: Abu Abd Allah, what has your stray camel done? Then we traveled on, and he would never catch up with me on the march but say: Peace be upon you, Abu Abd Allah, what has that stray camel done? When I saw that, I hastened to Madinah, avoiding the mosque and sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When that lengthened, I watched for an hour when the mosque was empty, came to the mosque and stood praying. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out suddenly from one of his chambers, prayed two light rakahs, and I lengthened hoping he would leave and let me be. He said: Lengthen, Abu Abd Allah, as long as you wish to lengthen, for I shall not stand until you finish. I said to myself: By Allah, I shall apologize to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and clear his chest. When he said: Peace be upon you, Abu Abd Allah, what has that stray camel done? I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, that camel has not strayed since I became Muslim. He said: May Allah have mercy on you — three times — then did not return to anything of what had been."
"4149","Narrated Ahmad ibn Hammad ibn Zughbah al-Misri, from Said ibn Abi Maryam, from Ibn Lahiah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Jafar, from Yaqub ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Said, from Khawwat ibn Jubayr, who said: A man died and appointed me executor; among what he bequeathed was his umm walad and a free wife. Words passed between the umm walad and the wife, and the wife said to her: O worthless one, tomorrow you will be seized by the ear and sold in the market. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She is not to be sold."
"4150","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qatawani, from Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Musaffar, from Abu Salih Khawwat ibn Jubayr, (ha) and narrated Musa ibn Zakariya al-Tustari, from Shabab al-Usfuri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Hashimi, from Khawwat ibn Salih ibn Khawwat ibn Jubayr, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I fell ill and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me; when I recovered he said: No sick person falls ill but he vows something and intends something of good — so fulfill for Allah what you promised Him."
"4151","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr al-Baghdadi, from Shabab al-Usfuri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Hashimi, from my father, from Salih ibn Khawwat ibn Salih Khawwat ibn Jubayr, from his father, from his grandfather, from Khawwat ibn Jubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"4152","Narrated Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar, from Muhammad ibn Ali al-Muqaddami, from Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mushir, from Abd Allah ibn Zayd, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Rabiah ibn Amr, from Khawwat ibn Jubayr, who said: I was praying when a man behind me said: Lighten, for we have need of you. I turned and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4153","Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, kunya Abu Abd Allah. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi, from Muslimah ibn Ishaq — or Maslamah ibn Ishaq — who said: I heard al-Rukayn Abu al-Rabi al-Fazari, from my uncle, from Abu Abd Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People are four, and deeds are six. Deeds: two necessitating, like for like, tenfold, and seven hundredfold. The two necessitating: whoever dies Muslim, Paradise is due for him; and whoever dies disbelieving, the Fire is due for him. Like for like: the servant intends a good deed and a good deed is written for him, and intends an evil deed and is recompensed only with its like. The servant does a good deed and ten are written for him; and the servant spends spending in the way of Allah and it is multiplied for him seven hundredfold. People are four: one given ease in this world and given ease in the Hereafter; one straitened in this world and given ease in the Hereafter; one given ease in this world and straitened in the Hereafter; and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter."
"4154","Narrated Ali ibn Said al-Razi, from Mihran ibn Abd Allah al-Razi, from al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Salman, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from al-Rabi ibn Umaylah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People are four and deeds are six. Of them: one given ease in this world and in the Hereafter; one given ease in this world and straitened in the Hereafter; one straitened in this world and given ease in the Hereafter; and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter. Deeds: two necessitating, like for like, tenfold, and seven hundredfold. The two necessitating: whoever dies associating nothing with Allah enters Paradise, and whoever dies associating something with Allah enters the Fire. Whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, a good deed is written for him; whoever does it, an evil deed is written against him. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, a good deed is written for him; if he does it, tenfold is written for him. Spending in the way of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, is seven hundredfold."
"4155","Narrated Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari, from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from Shayban, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from his father, from his uncle Yusayr ibn Umaylah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are four and deeds are six. People: one given ease in this world and the Hereafter; one given ease in this world and straitened in the Hereafter; one straitened in this world and given ease in the Hereafter; and one wretched in this world and the Hereafter. Deeds: two necessitating, like for like, tenfold, and seven hundredfold. The two necessitating: whoever dies Muslim or believing, associating nothing with Allah, Paradise is due for him; and whoever dies disbelieving, the Fire is due for him. Whoever intends a good deed and does not do it, and Allah knows his heart has conceived it and is keen upon it, a good deed is written for him and nothing is multiplied. Whoever intends an evil deed and does not do it, it is not written against him; whoever does it, one is written against him and nothing is multiplied against him. Whoever does a good deed, ten the like of it are his; and whoever spends spending in the way of Allah, it is his at seven hundredfold."
"4156","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr, from Abu al-Nadr, from al-Ashjai, from Sufyan, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from his father, from Yusayr ibn Umaylah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4157","Narrated Ubayd Allah ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi, from Zaidah, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from his father, from Yusayr ibn Umaylah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: People are four and deeds are six: one given ease in this world and the Hereafter; one given ease in this world and straitened in the Hereafter; one straitened in this world and straitened in the Hereafter; and one given ease in the Hereafter and straitened in this world. Deeds are six: two necessitating, like for like, tenfold, and seven hundredfold. Whoever dies Muslim or believing, associating nothing with Allah, is admitted to Paradise; and whoever dies disbelieving is admitted to the Fire. Whoever intends a good deed until his heart conceives it, a good deed is written for him, not multiplied. Whoever does an evil deed, one evil deed is written against him, not multiplied against him. Whoever does a good deed, ten the like of it are written for him; and whoever spends spending in the way of Allah, seven hundredfold is written for him."
"4158","Narrated Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib, from Abd Allah ibn Salih al-Ijli, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What a man you are, were it not for two traits in you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are they? He said: You let your lower garment trail and you let your hair hang loose. I said: No harm shall return — I shall not repeat. He said: So he cut his hair and raised his lower garment."
"4159","Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, from Abu Ishaq, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man: trailing the lower garment and letting the hair hang."
"4160","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Yahya al-Himmani, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Ishaq and Abu Husayn, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent youth Khuraym would be, if he took from his hair and shortened his lower garment."
"4161","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah ibn Man al-Masudi, from my father, from his father, from his grandfather, from al-Amash, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Khuraym ibn Fatik, were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man. He said: What are they — may my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah — one alone suffices me? He said: Letting your hair grow full and trailing your lower garment. So Khuraym went off, cut his hair and shortened his lower garment."
"4162","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Raqqi, from Abu al-Jawwab, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from al-Amash, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Khuraym ibn Fatik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4163","Narrated Hajib ibn Arkin al-Farghani, from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mufaddal al-Harrani, from Yunus ibn Bukayr, from al-Masudi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ayman ibn Khuraym ibn Fatik, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What an excellent youth Khuraym would be, if he shortened his hair and raised his lower garment. He said: Khuraym said: My hair shall not pass my ears, nor my lower garment my ankles."
"4164","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (ha) and narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, from Ali ibn al-Madini, (ha) and narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from my father, all saying: narrated Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Sufyan ibn Ziyad al-Usfuri, from his father, from Habib ibn al-Numan al-Asadi, from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer; when he finished, standing, he said: False testimony has been equated with associating with Allah — three times — then recited this verse: And avoid false speech, inclining to Allah, not associating with Him."
"4165","Narrated Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Dimashqi, from Hisham ibn Ammar, (ha) and narrated Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawwazi al-Basri, from al-Walid ibn Shuja, both saying: narrated al-Walid ibn Muslim, from Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from his father, from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The people of Sham are the whip of Allah in His land; He takes vengeance through them upon whom He wills of His servants, and it is forbidden for their hypocrites to prevail over their believers, and they die only in grief and sorrow."
"4166","Narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Raqqi, from al-Ala ibn Hilal, from my father, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Amr ibn Wabisah, from his father, from Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi of Banu Amr ibn Asad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will be tribulation; the sleeper therein is better than the sitter, the sitter therein is better than the walker, the walker therein is better than the runner, and the runner is better than the rider."
"4167","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami, from Abd Allah ibn Musa al-Iskandarani, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Khuraym ibn Fatik said to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: O Commander of the Believers, shall I not tell you how my Islam began? He said: Yes indeed. He said: While I was roaming seeking camels of mine, and I was upon their trail, night fell upon me at Abraq al-Azzaf. I called out at the top of my voice: I seek refuge with the mighty one of this valley from the fools of his people — when a caller called out, and I was seized with severe fright. When I came to myself — then I followed my mount. He said: Then he followed me saying — He said: Then I entered Madinah, that being Friday. I looked into the mosque, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, came out to me and said: Enter, may Allah have mercy on you, for your Islam has reached us. I said: I do not do purification well, so he taught me. I entered the mosque and saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon the pulpit preaching, as though the full moon, saying: No Muslim performs ablution well, then prays a prayer guarding it and comprehending it, but enters Paradise. Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: You shall bring proof of this or I shall make an example of you. The elder of Quraysh, Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, testified for me, and he accepted his testimony."
"4168","Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Muhammad ibn Tasnim al-Hadrami, from Muhammad ibn Khalifah al-Asadi, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad, from his father, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said one day to Ibn Abbas: Narrate to me a hadith that pleases me. He said: Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi told me, who said: I went out seeking camels and found them at al-Abraq al-Azzaf; I hobbled them and pillowed the foreleg of one of them — that being soon after the emergence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I said: I seek refuge with the great one of this valley — and so they used to do in the Jahiliyyah — when a caller called to me saying — He said: I said — He said: I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Malik ibn Malik; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me over the jinn of the people of Najd. He said: I said: Had I one to suffice me for these camels of mine, I would come to him and believe in him. He said: I shall suffice you for them until I deliver them to your family safe, if Allah wills. So I tied one of them, then came to Madinah and found the people on Friday in prayer. I said: They will finish their prayer, then I shall enter — and I was weary, making my mount kneel, when Abu Dharr, may Allah have mercy on him, came out to me and said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says to you: Enter. So I entered; when he saw me he said: What did the elder do who guaranteed you he would deliver your camels to your family safe? Indeed he delivered them to your family safe? He said: I said: May Allah have mercy on him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes indeed, may Allah have mercy on him. He said: I testify there is no god but Allah — and his Islam was good."
"4169","Khuraym ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam al-Tai. Narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad and Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar, (ha) and narrated Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari, all saying: narrated Abu al-Sukayn Zakariya ibn Yahya, from the uncle of my father Zahr ibn Hisn, from his grandfather Humayd ibn Munhib, who said: Khuraym ibn Aws ibn Harithah ibn Lam said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, may Allah have mercy on him, said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to praise you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Bring it — may Allah not break your mouth. So al-Abbas began to say his verses."
"4170","Narrated Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hammad al-Barbari and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: narrated Abu al-Sukayn, from the uncle of my father Zahr ibn Hisn, from his grandfather Humayd ibn Munhib, who said: Khuraym ibn Aws said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: This al-Hirah, the white one, has been raised up to me; and this al-Shayma bint Buqaylah al-Azdiyyah upon a gray mule, wrapped in a black veil. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if we enter al-Hirah and I find her in this state, is she mine? He said: She is yours. Then the Arabs apostatized and none of Tayyi apostatized. We fought Banu Asad, among them Tulayhah ibn Khuwaylid al-Faqasi, and Khalid ibn al-Walid praised us — among what he said of us: and utter darkness. Then Khalid marched to Musaylimah and we marched with him; when we finished with Musaylimah and his companions, we turned toward Basra and met Hurmuz at Kazimah with a great host — none more hostile to the Arabs than Hurmuz. Abu al-Sukayn said: Of him the proverb is coined; the Arabs say: You are more disbelieving than Hurmuz. Khalid ibn al-Walid came forth to him and called to single combat; Hurmuz came forth to him and Khalid killed him, may Allah be pleased with him, and wrote of that to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who gave him his spoils. The cap of Hurmuz reached one hundred thousand dirhams — the Persians, when a man rose eminent among them, made his cap worth one hundred thousand dirhams. Then we marched by the way of al-Taff until we entered al-Hirah; the first to meet us therein was Shayma bint Buqaylah al-Azdiyyah upon a gray mule of hers with a black veil, as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said. I clung to her and said: This one the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me. Khalid called me for proof of her, so I brought it to him and he handed her to me. Her brother Abd al-Masih came down to us and said to me: Sell her to me. I said: By Allah, I shall not lower her below ten hundred by anything. He paid me a thousand dirhams. It was said to me: Had you said a hundred thousand, he would have paid it to you. I said: I did not think wealth greater than ten hundred. And it reached me in other than this hadith that the two witnesses were Muhammad ibn Maslamah and Abd Allah ibn Umar."
"4171","Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari — he is Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah ibn Qahlan ibn Harithah ibn Ghifar. Narrated Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri, from Said ibn Abi Maryam, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Harmalah, from Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami, that Khufaf ibn Ima al-Ghifari informed him — and he had companionship — that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in one of the prayers; when he raised his head from bowing he said: O Allah, curse Lihyan, Ril, Dhakwan and Usayyah — Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger; and Ghifar, may Allah forgive her; and Aslam, may Allah grant her safety."
"4172","Narrated Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki, from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, from Abu Damrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Hanzalah ibn Ali, from Khufaf ibn Ima al-Ghifari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a prayer and mentioned the like of it."
"4173","Narrated Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri, from my father, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Hanzalah ibn Ali, from Khufaf ibn Ima, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4174","Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Hanzalah ibn Ali, from Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in a prayer: O Allah, curse Banu Lihyan, Ril, Dhakwan and Usayyah — they disobeyed Allah; and Ghifar, may Allah forgive her; and Aslam, may Allah grant her safety."
"4175","Narrated Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti, from Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, (ha) and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami, from Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr; when he raised his head from the last rakah he said: May Allah curse Lihyan, Ril, Dhakwan and Usayyah — Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger; Aslam, may Allah grant her safety; and Ghifar, may Allah forgive her. Then he fell prostrate. When he finished the prayer he turned to the people with his face and said: O people, it is not I who said this, but Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said it."
"4176","Narrated Abu Yazid al-Qaratisi, from Hajjaj ibn Ibrahim al-Azraq, from Ismail ibn Jafar, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah ibn Harmalah, from al-Harith ibn Khufaf ibn Ima, who said: Khufaf ibn Ima said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, then raised his head and said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive her; and Aslam, may Allah grant her safety; and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. O Allah, curse Banu Lihyan, Ril and Dhakwan. Then he fell prostrate. Khufaf said: The cursing of the disbelievers was made on account of that."
"4177","Narrated Idris ibn Jafar al-Attar, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah ibn Harmalah, from al-Harith ibn Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, (ha) and narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (ha) and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, both saying: narrated Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Khalid ibn Abd Allah ibn Harmalah, from al-Harith ibn Khufaf ibn Ima, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed, then raised his head and said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive her; and Aslam, may Allah grant her safety; and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. O Allah, curse Banu Lihyan; O Allah, curse Ril and Dhakwan. Allah is Greatest. Then he fell prostrate."
"4178","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Ubayd ibn Yaish, from Yunus ibn Bukayr, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Miqsam, from Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat at the end of his prayer, he would point with his forefinger; the polytheists would say: He bewitches with it — and they lied; rather it is tawhid."
"4179","Khashkhash al-Anbari. Narrated Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from my father, (ha) and narrated al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati, from Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti, (ha) and narrated Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati, from Said ibn Sulayman, all saying: narrated Hushaym, from Yunus, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, that al-Khashkhash al-Anbari said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my son, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He does not offend on your account, nor do you offend on his."
"4180","Khalifah ibn Adi al-Ansari, a Badri. Narrated Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Dirar ibn Surad, from Ali ibn Hashim, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father, concerning the naming of those of the Ansar who stood with Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Khalifah ibn Adi of Banu Bayadah, a Badri."
"4181","Khizam Abu Wadiah. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Ali ibn al-Mundhir, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi, sons of Yazid ibn Harithah, both saying: Khizam married his daughter, unwilling, to a man, she being previously married. She came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and he annulled her marriage."
"4182","Khirashah al-Muharibi. Narrated Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Musa al-Antaki, from Yaqub ibn Kab al-Halabi, from Muhammad ibn Himyar, (ha) and narrated Abdan ibn Ahmad, from Yahya ibn Uthman al-Himsi, from my father, from Muhammad ibn Muhajir — both from Thabit ibn Ajlan, from Abu Kathir al-Muharibi, who said: I heard Khirashah al-Muharibi say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulations; the sleeper therein is better than the wakeful, the sitter therein is better than the stander, the stander therein is better than the walker, and the walker is better than the runner. When it comes upon one of you, let him walk with his sword to al-Safa and strike it until it breaks, then lie down until it clears as it clears."
"4183","Khirashah ibn al-Harith. Narrated Abu al-Zinba Rawh ibn al-Faraj, from Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani, from Ibn Lahiah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Khirashah ibn al-Harithah, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall witness one killed while held captive, lest he be killed wronged and wrath descend upon them and strike him with them."
"4184","Al-Khirbaq. Narrated Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal, from Yazid ibn Zuray, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salam in three rakahs of al-Asr, then entered. A man called al-Khirbaq, long of arms, stood up to him and said: Has the prayer been shortened, O Messenger of Allah? He came out angry, dragging his cloak, and said: Is he truthful? They said: Yes. So he stood and prayed that rakah."
"4185","Khidash Abu Salamah al-Sulami. Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik, from my father, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Asim, from his father, who said: Abu Salamah al-Sulami alighted upon us and we hosted him two months."
"4186","Narrated Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, from Abd Allah ibn Raja, from Shayban, from Mansur, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali, from Urfutah al-Sulami, from Khidash Abu Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I enjoin a man concerning his mother; I enjoin a man concerning his father; I enjoin a man concerning his patron who is next to him, even if harm upon him annoys him."
"4187","Narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Rahawayh, from my father, (ha) and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Jarir, from Mansur, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali, from Khidash Abu Salamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I enjoin a man concerning his mother; I enjoin a man concerning his father; I enjoin a man concerning his patron who is next to him, even if harm from him annoys him."
"4188","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Sharik, from Mansur, from Ubayd Allah ibn Ali, from Abu Salamah al-Sulami, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I enjoin a man concerning his mother; I enjoin a man concerning his mother; I enjoin a man concerning his father; I enjoin a man concerning his patron who is next to him, even if harm upon him therein annoys him."
"4189","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Jubarah ibn Mughallis, from Ubaydah ibn Humayd, from Mansur, from Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn Urfutah, from Abu Salamah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4190","Khazraj al-Ansari. Narrated Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf al-Tustari, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Aqil, from Ismail ibn Aban, from Amr ibn Shamir al-Jufi, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, who said: I heard al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj say: My father told me, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say — and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the Angel of Death, peace be upon him, at the head of a man of the Ansar, and said: O Angel of Death, be gentle with my companion, for he is a believer. The Angel of Death, peace be upon him, said: Be of good cheer and cool your eye; know that I am gentle with every believer. Know, O Muhammad, that I seize the soul of the son of Adam, and when one of his family wails, I stand in the house with his soul and say: What is this wailer? By Allah, we wronged him not, nor did we precede his term nor hasten his decree; we have no sin in seizing him. If you are pleased with what Allah has done, you are rewarded; if you grieve and rage, you sin and bear burden. You have no reproach against us, and we shall return to you again and again — so beware. There is no household, O Muhammad — of hair or mud, land or sea, plain or mountain — but I peruse them every day and night, until I know their small and great better than they know themselves. By Allah, O Muhammad, had I wished to seize the soul of a gnat, I could not until Allah Himself permits its seizure. Jafar said: It reached me that he peruses them only at the times of prayer; when he looks at death, whoever guarded the prayers, the angel draws near him, repels Satan from him, and the angel prompts him: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah — and that is the great state."
"4191","Khawt ibn Abd al-Uzza — and it is said Hawt. Narrated Muadh ibn al-Muthanna, from Musaddad, from Abd al-Warith, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Khawt ibn Abd al-Uzza, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded cutting off the bell."
"4192","Narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Yahya al-Himmani, from Abd al-Warith ibn Said, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Abu Buraydah, from Khawt ibn Abd al-Uzza, that he told me that a caravan of Mudar passed with a bell in it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a caravan in which there is a bell."
"4193","Khubayb ibn Adi al-Ansari. Narrated Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Amr ibn Abi Sufyan al-Thaqafi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched a reconnaissance patrol and put Asim ibn Thabit in command over them — he being the grandfather of Asim ibn Umar. They set out until, on part of the way between Usfan and Makkah, they alighted; they were mentioned to a clan of Hudhayl called Banu Lihyan. They followed them with close to a hundred archers, tracked their traces until they alighted at a stopping place and found therein date stones they had provisioned of the dates of Madinah. They said: These are of the dates of Yathrib. They followed their traces until they caught them. When Asim ibn Thabit and his companions perceived them, they took refuge on a hill and the people surrounded them. They said: You have covenant and pact — if you come down to us, we shall not kill any man of you. Asim ibn Thabit said: As for me, I shall not come down under the protection of a disbeliever. O Allah, inform Your Messenger of us. He said: They fought them and shot them until they killed Asim among seven men. Khubayb ibn Adi and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah remained until they sold them both at Makkah. Khubayb was bought by the sons of al-Harith ibn Amir ibn Nawfal — and he had killed al-Harith on the day of Badr. He remained with them captive until, when they resolved to kill him, he borrowed a razor from one of the daughters of al-Harith, and she lent it to him to shave with. He said: I was heedless of a boy of mine; he toddled to him until he reached him. She said: He took him and placed him upon his thigh; when she saw him she was frightened with a fright he perceived in her, the razor in his hand. He said: Do you fear I shall kill him? I would not do it, if Allah wills. He said: She used to say: I never saw a captive better than Khubayb; I saw him eating of a bunch of grapes, and there was no fruit in Makkah that day, while he was bound in iron — it was only provision Allah granted him. He said: Then they took him out of the Sanctuary to kill him. He said: Let me pray two rakahs. He prayed two rakahs, then said: Were it not that you think what is in me is dread of death, I would add. He was the first to institute the two rakahs at killing. Then he said: O Allah, count them in number. Then he said his verses. Then Uqbah ibn al-Harith stood to him. He said: And he killed him. He said: Quraysh sent to Asim that they be brought something of his body by which they would know him — and he had killed a great one of their great ones on the day of Badr — so Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, sent to him like a canopy of hornets that shielded him from their messengers, and they could take nothing of him."
"4194","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim, from Ibrahim ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Umar ibn Asid ibn Jariyah al-Thaqafi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched ten men as scouts, among them Khubayb ibn Adi and Zayd ibn al-Dathinah — then he mentioned the like of the hadith of Mamar."
"4195","Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam and Abdan ibn Ahmad, both saying: narrated Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Jafar ibn Awn, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from al-Zuhri, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him alone as a scout toward Quraysh. He said: I came to the wood of Khubayb fearing watchers; I climbed it and loosed Khubayb, and he fell to the ground. I withdrew not far, then I saw Khubayb as though the earth had swallowed him; Khubayb has not been seen to this hour. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said: Jafar ibn Awn had said: from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, from his grandfather."
"4196","Khubayb ibn Isaf Abu Abd al-Rahman ibn Utbah ibn Amr. Narrated Ubayd ibn Ghannam, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, (ha) and narrated al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, both saying: narrated Yazid ibn Harun, from Mustalim ibn Said, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khubayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out intending a direction; I and a man of my people came and said: We dislike that our people witness a witnessing we do not witness with them. He said: Have you become Muslim? We said: No. He said: We do not seek aid from polytheists. He said: So we became Muslim and witnessed with him. A man of the polytheists struck me upon my shoulder; I killed him and married his daughter after that. She used to say: May you never lose a man who adorned you with this sash. I would say to her: May you never lose a man who hastened your father to the Fire."
"4197","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami, from Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Mustalim ibn Said, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khubayb al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I and a man of my people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before we became Muslim, and said: We are ashamed that our people witness a witnessing we do not witness with them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Have you become Muslim? We said: No. He said: I do not seek aid from polytheists against polytheists. So we became Muslim and witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4198","Narrated Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Abbas al-Asbahani, from Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Sad al-Dashtaki, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from Mustalim ibn Said, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Khubayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I do not seek aid from a polytheist."
"4199","Chapter of Dal. Dihyah ibn Khalifah al-Kalbi. Narrated Muttalib ibn Shuayb al-Azdi, from Abd Allah ibn Salih, from al-Layth, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Mansur al-Kalbi, that Dihyah ibn Khalifah went out from his village at Damascus, al-Mazzah, to the measure of the village of Uqbah in Ramadan, then broke fast and the people broke fast with him, while others disliked breaking fast. When he returned to his village he said: By Allah, I saw today a matter I never thought I would see: people turned away from the guidance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions — saying that of those who fasted. Then he said at that: O Allah, take me to You."
"4200","Narrated Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari, both saying: narrated Yahya al-Himmani, from Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Dihyah al-Kalbi, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Caesar, sovereign of Byzantium, with a letter. I said: Seek permission for the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Caesar was approached and told: At the door is a man claiming he is the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They were alarmed at that. He said: Admit him. He admitted me to him, with his patricians about him. I gave him the letter and it was read to him; in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate — from Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, to Caesar, sovereign of Byzantium. A red, blue-eyed, lank-haired nephew of his snorted and said: Do not read the letter today — he began with himself, and wrote sovereign of Byzantium; he did not write king of Byzantium. He said: The letter was read until it was finished of them. Then he commanded them and they left him. Then he sent to me and I entered to him; he questioned me and I informed him. He sent to the bishop, who entered to him — he being the master of their affair, whose opinion and word they followed. When he read the letter, the bishop said: By Allah, this is he whom Musa and Isa gave us glad tidings of, whom we awaited. Caesar said: What do you command me? He said: As for me, I believe him and follow him. Caesar said: I know it is so, but I cannot do it — if I do, my kingdom goes and the Byzantines kill me."
